msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.A2_AGRICULTURALNOTES.TITLE"
msgid "Agricultural Notes"
msgstr "農業筆記"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.A2_B327.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.A2_B327.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "I'm starting my new job at Gravitas today. I'm... well, I'm nervous.\n\nIt turns out they hired a bunch of new people - I guess they're expanding - and most of them are about my age, but I'm the only one that hasn't done my doctorate. They all call me \"Mister\" Kraus and it's the <i>worst</i>.\n\nI have no idea where I'll find the time to do my PhD while working a full time job.\n------------------\n"
msgstr "我今天開始在「引力科技」的新工作了。我... 該怎麼說呢，有點緊張。\n\n看來他們招募了一批新人——我猜他們正在擴大編制吧——大多都跟我年紀差不多，但我卻是唯一一個還沒有拿到博士學位的人。他們都叫我 Kraus「先生」，這感覺簡直<b>糟透了</b>。\n\n我真不知道一邊做著全職工作，一邊要怎麼擠出時間來把我的博士學位搞定。\n------------------\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.A2_B327.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.A2_B327.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "<i>I screwed up so much today.</i>\n\nAt one point I spaced on the formula for calculating the volume of a cone. They must have thought I was completely useless.\n\nThe only time I knew what I was doing was when I helped an older coworker figure out her dumb old email.\n\nPeople say education isn't so important as long as you've got the skills, but there's things my colleagues know that I just <i>don't</i>. They're not mean about it or anything, it's just so frustrating. I feel dumb when I talk to them!\n\nI bet they're gonna realize soon that I don't belong here, and then I'll be fired for sure. Man... I'm still paying off my student loans (WITH international fees), I <i>can't</i> lose this income.\n------------------\n"
msgstr "<b>我今天真的搞砸慘了。</b>\n\n有一次，我居然忘記計算圓錐體體積的公式，腦子一片空白。他們一定覺得我完全是個廢物。\n\n我唯一感覺自己還能派上用場的時候，是幫一位資深同事搞定她那個超老舊的電子郵件問題。\n\n大家都說「有能力比學歷重要」，但我的那些同事們知道的事情，我就是<b>不知道</b>。\n\n他們人沒有惡意啦，但這真的太令人挫敗了。跟他們講話的時候，我都覺得自己好笨！\n\n我打賭，他們很快就會發現我不屬於這裡，然後我一定會被開除。天啊... 我的學貸還沒繳完耶（還包括國際學費），我<b>絕對不能</b>失去這份收入。\n------------------\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.A2_B327.BODY.CONTAINER3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.A2_B327.BODY.CONTAINER3"
msgid "Dr. Sklodowska's been really nice and welcoming since I started working here. Sometimes she comes and sits with me in the cafeteria. The food she brings from home smells like old feet but she chats with me about what new research papers we're each reading and it's very kind.\n\nShe tells me the fact I got hired without a doctorate means I must be very smart, and management must see something in me.\n\nI'm not sure I believe her but it's nice to hear something that counters little voice in my head anyway.\n------------------\n"
msgstr "自從我來這裡工作後，Sklodowska 博士一直對我很好、也很熱情。她有時候會來自助餐廳跟我一起坐。她從家裡帶來的午餐聞起來像舊襪子一樣，但她會跟我聊聊我們各自正在讀什麼新的研究論文，這真的很窩心。\n\n她告訴我，能沒靠博士學位就被錄取，就代表我一定很聰明，高層肯定在我身上看到了什麼特質。\n\n我不太確定該不該相信她，但無論如何，能聽到一些能反駁我腦中那個小聲音的話，感覺真好。\n------------------\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.A2_B327.BODY.CONTAINER4
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.A2_B327.BODY.CONTAINER4"
msgid "It's been about a week and a half and I think I'm finally starting to settle in. I'm feeling a lot better about my position - some of the senior scientists have even started using my ideas in the lab.\n\nDr. Sklodowska might have been right, my anxiety was just growing pains. This is my first real job and I guess afraid to let myself believe I could really, actually do it, just in case it went wrong.\n\nI think I want to buy Dr. Sklowdoska a digital reader for her books and papers as a thank-you one day, if I ever pay off my student loans.\n\nONCE I pay off my student loans.\n------------------\n"
msgstr "已經過了一個半禮拜，我想我終於開始適應了。我對自己的職位感覺好很多－一些資深科學家甚至已經開始在實驗室裡採用我的點子了。\n\nSklodowska 博士說得可能沒錯，我的焦慮只是成長的陣痛期。這是我第一份真正的工作，我猜我只是不敢讓自己相信我真的、真的能做到，怕萬一搞砸了怎麼辦。\n\n我想有一天，等我還清學貸後，我想買一個電子閱讀器給 Sklowdoska 博士，讓她用來看書和論文，當作是感謝。\n\n<B>等我還清學貸的那一天</B>。\n------------------\n"

