#. STRINGS.CODEX.B6_TIMEMUSINGS.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.B6_TIMEMUSINGS.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "When we discuss Time as a concrete aspect of the universe, not seconds on a clock or perceptions of the mind, it is important first of all to establish that we are talking about a unique dimension that layers into the three physical dimensions of space: length, width, depth.\n\nWe conceive of Real Time as a straight line, one dimensional, uncurved and stretching forward infinitely. This is referred to as the \"Arrow of Time\".\n\nLogically this Arrow can move only forward and can never be reversed, as such a reversal would break the natural laws of the universe. Effect would precede cause and universal entropy would be undone in a blatant violation of the Second Law.\n\nStill, one can't help but wonder; what if the Arrow's trajectory could be curved? What if it could be redirected, guided, or loosed? What if we could create Time's Bow?"
msgstr "當我們討論時間作為宇宙的具體面向時，不是時鐘上的一秒或是心裡的感覺，首先，重要的是確定我們在討論一個獨特的維度，將空間分成三個物理層面：長度，寬度，深度。\n\n我們將真實的時間當作一條直線，一維、不會彎曲且無限延伸的直線。這被稱為「時光之箭」。\n\n邏輯上，這支箭只能往前移動並不能逆轉，\n因為這樣的逆轉會破壞宇宙的規律。\n\n在公然違反第二定律的情況下，影響會優先於起因並且宇宙的熵會消失。\n\n但是，人們還是不禁想問；如果箭的軌跡可以彎曲會怎麼樣？如果可以重新定向、引導或變寬會怎麼樣？如果我們可以創造時光之弓會怎麼樣？"

