#. STRINGS.CODEX.B8_MAGAZINEARTICLE.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.B8_MAGAZINEARTICLE.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<b>Incredible Technology From Independent Lab Harnesses Time into Energy</b>"
msgstr "<b>來自獨立實驗室令人難以置信的科技－將時間轉變成能源</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.B8_MAGAZINEARTICLE.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.B8_MAGAZINEARTICLE.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "Scientists from the recently founded Gravitas Facility have unveiled their first technology prototype, dubbed the \"Temporal Bow\". It is a device which manipulates the 4th dimension to generate infinite, clean and renewable energy.\n\nWhile it may sound like something from science fiction, facility founder Dr. Jacquelyn Stern confirms that it is very much real.\n\n\"It has already been demonstrated that Newton's Second Law of Motion can be violated by negative mass superfluids under the correct lab conditions,\" she says.\n\n\"If the Laws of Motion can be bent and altered, why not the Laws of Thermodynamics? That was the main intent behind this project.\"\n\nThe Temporal Bow works by rapidly vibrating sections of the 4th dimension to send small quantities of mass forward and backward in time, generating massive amounts of energy with virtually no waste.\n\n\"The fantastic thing about using the 4th dimension as fuel,\" says Stern, \"is that it is really, categorically infinite\".\n\nFor those eagerly awaiting the prospect of human time travel, don't get your hopes up just yet. The Facility says that although they have successfully transported matter through time, the technology was expressly developed for the purpose of energy generation and is ill-equipped for human transportation."
msgstr "最近成立的「引力科技」的科學家們推出了第一個技術原型，他們稱之為「時光之弓」，一種操縱第四維度的設備可產生無限、乾淨與可再生的能源。\n\n聽起來有點像科幻小說裡有的東西。設施的創辦者 Jacquelyn Stern 博士，證實這非常的真實。\n\n她說：「已經證明了，在正確的實驗條件之下，負質量超流體會違反牛頓第二運動定律」。\n\n「如果運動定律可以彎曲和改變，那熱力學為什麼不行呢？這就是此計劃背後隱含的意義。」\n\n時光之弓的原理的是在第四維度內，透過快速震動在時光內使少量物質向前或向後移動，產生幾乎沒有浪費的大量能源。\n\nStern 說：「這就是使用第四維度作為燃料的神奇之處－真實，絕對無限」。\n\n對於那些等待渴望時光旅行的人，暫時不要抱任何期待。\n\n該設施說雖然他們成功的讓物質傳送了一段時間，不過這項技術是專為生產能源而開發的，在人類運輸方面的仍缺少相應裝備。"

