msgstr "加密等級：三"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.B9_TELEPORTATION.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.B9_TELEPORTATION.TITLE"
msgid "Memory Breakthrough"
msgstr "記憶突破"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BALMLILY.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BALMLILY.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Balm Lily naturally contains high vitamin concentrations and produces acids similar in molecular makeup to acetylsalicylic acid (commonly known as aspirin).\n\nAs a result, the plant is ideal both for boosting immune systems and treating a variety of common maladies such as pain and fever."
msgstr "香水百合天然含有高濃度的維他命，與生產在分子結構上與水楊酸相近的酸性物質（俗稱阿斯匹靈）。\n\n因此，這株植物是增強免疫系統與治療常見疾病（像是疼痛與發燒）的首選。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BALMLILY.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BALMLILY.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Medicinal Herb"
msgstr "草藥"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BALMLILY.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BALMLILY.TITLE"
msgid "Balm Lily"
msgstr "香水百合"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASIC_FABRIC.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASIC_FABRIC.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "A ball of raw cellulose harvested from a <link=\"BASICFABRICPLANT\">Thimble Reed</link>.\n\nIt is used in the production of <link=\"EQUIPMENT\">Clothing</link> and textiles."
msgstr "一團從<link=\"BASICFABRICPLANT\">頂針蘆葦</link>上收成的纖維素原料。\n\n它可用於生產<link=\"EQUIPMENT\">服裝</link>和紡織品。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASIC_FABRIC.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASIC_FABRIC.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Textile Ingredient"
msgstr "紡織品配方"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASIC_FABRIC.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASIC_FABRIC.TITLE"
msgid "Reed Fiber"
msgstr "蘆葦纖維"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASICBOOSTER.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASICBOOSTER.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "A supplement that minorly reduces the chance of contracting a <style=\"KKeyword\">Germ</style>-based <link=\"DISEASE\">Disease</link>.\n\nMust be taken daily."
msgstr "一種能輕微降低感染<style=\"KKeyword\">病菌</style>性<link=\"DISEASE\">疾病</link>機率的補充劑。\n\n必須每日服用。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASICBOOSTER.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASICBOOSTER.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Health Supplement"
msgstr "保健品"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASICBOOSTER.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASICBOOSTER.TITLE"
msgid "Vitamin Chews"
msgstr "維生素咀嚼錠"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASICCURE.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASICCURE.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Duplicants can take this to cure themselves of minor <style=\"KKeyword\">Germ</style>-based <link=\"DISEASE\">Diseases</link>.\n\nCurative Tablets are very effective against <link=\"FOODSICKNESS\">Food Poisoning</link>."
msgstr "複製人可以服用此藥以治癒輕微的<style=\"KKeyword\">病菌</style>性<link=\"DISEASE\">疾病</link>。\n\n治療藥片對抗<link=\"FOODSICKNESS\">腸病毒</link>非常有效。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASICCURE.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASICCURE.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Self-Administered Medicine"
msgstr "自行服用藥物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASICCURE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASICCURE.TITLE"
msgid "Curative Tablet"
msgstr "治療藥片"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASICRADPILL.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASICRADPILL.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "A supplement that speeds up the rate at which a Duplicant body absorbs radiation, allowing them to manage increased radiation exposure.\n\nMust be taken daily."
msgstr "一種能加速複製人身體處理輻射速度的補充劑，使其能應對增加的輻射暴露。\n\n必須每日服用。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASICRADPILL.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASICRADPILL.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Radiation Recovery"
msgstr "輻射恢復"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BASICRADPILL.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BASICRADPILL.TITLE"
msgid "Basic Rad Pill"
msgstr "基本輻射藥片"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Beetas are insectoid creatures that enjoy a symbiotic relationship with the radioactive environment they thrive in.\n\nMuch like the honey bee gathers nectar and processes it to honey, the Beeta turns <link=\"URANIUMORE\">Uranium Ore</link> into <link=\"ENRICHEDURANIUM\">Enriched Uranium</link> through a complex process of isotope separation inside the Beeta Hive.\n\nWhen first observing the Beeta's enrichment process, many scientists note with surprise just how much more efficient the cooperative combination of insect and hive is when compared to even the most advanced industrial processes."
msgstr "輻射蜂是一種類昆蟲生物，與牠們賴以生存的放射性環境有著共生關係。\n\n就像蜜蜂採集花蜜並將其加工成蜂蜜一樣，輻射蜂通過輻射蜂巢內複雜的同位素分離過程，將<link=\"URANIUMORE\">鈾礦</link>轉化成<link=\"ENRICHEDURANIUM\">濃縮鈾</link>。\n\n當第一次觀察輻射蜂的濃縮過程時，許多科學家驚訝地注意到，即使與最先進的工業流程相比，昆蟲與蜂巢的結合工作效率也要高的多。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Aggressive Critter"
msgstr "侵略性動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.TITLE"
msgid "Beeta"
msgstr "輻射蜂"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.HEADER_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.HEADER_1"
msgid "Basic Needs"
msgstr "基本需求"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.HEADER_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.HEADER_2"
msgid "Worker Optimization"
msgstr "工作最佳化"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.PARAGRAPH_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.PARAGRAPH_1"
msgid "<link=\"POWER\">Power</link>: Bionic Duplicants run on portable <link=\"ELECTROBANK\">Power Banks</link> that they automatically replace during scheduled Downtime. If power banks are depleted, the Bionic Duplicant will become Powerless and may perish if they deplete their <link=\"OXYGEN\">Oxygen</link> tanks before being rebooted.\n\n<link=\"GUNKEMPTIER\">Gunk Extractors</link>: Bionic systems must dispose of built-up <link=\"LIQUIDGUNK\">Gunk</link> every {time}, or risk making a mess. If there are no purpose-built extractors available, Bionic Duplicants will clog a nearby <link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSTOILETTYPE\">Toilet</link>.\n\n<link=\"BUILDCATEGORYOXYGEN\">Oxygen</link>: Bionic Duplicants ventilate their mechanisms using internal <link=\"OXYGEN\">Oxygen</link> tanks. These must be refilled every {number} to prevent suffocation. They do not produce <link=\"CARBONDIOXIDE\">Carbon Dioxide</link>.\n\n<link=\"LUBRICATINGOIL\">Gear Oil</link>: Maintaining efficient operation of bionic systems requires visits to the <link=\"OILCHANGER\">Lubrication Station</link> or use of <link=\"LUBRICATIONSTICK\">Gear Balm</link>. If neither are available, workers slow down to avoid grinding gears.\n\n"
msgstr "<link=\"POWER\">電源</link>：仿生複製人使用攜帶式<link=\"ELECTROBANK\">行動電源</link>運行，並在預定的休息時間內自動更換行動電源。如果行動電源耗盡，仿生複製人將變得無法運作，並且如果在重新啟動之前耗盡其<link=\"OXYGEN\">氧氣</link>罐，仿生複製人可能會死亡。\n\n<link=\"GUNKEMPTIER\">黏渣提取器</link>：仿生系統上堆積的<link=\"LIQUIDGUNK\">黏渣</link>必須每隔 {time}清除一次，否則可能會隨處製造髒亂。如果沒有專門製造的提取器，仿生複製人將會堵塞附近的<link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSTOILETTYPE\">廁所</link>。\n\n<link=\"BUILDCATEGORYOXYGEN\">氧氣</link>：仿生複製人使用自身攜帶的<link=\"OXYGEN\">氧氣</link>罐進行機制通風。每隔 {number}必須重新填充一次，否則他們會窒息。他們不會產生<link=\"CARBONDIOXIDE\">二氧化碳</link>。\n\n<link=\"LUBRICATINGOIL\">齒輪油</link>：維持仿生系統的有效運作需要拜訪<link=\"OILCHANGER\">潤滑站</link>或使用<link=\"LUBRICATIONSTICK\">齒輪油</link>。如果兩者皆無，仿生複製人就會放慢速度，以避免齒輪磨損。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.PARAGRAPH_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.PARAGRAPH_2"
msgid "<link=\"BOOSTER\">Boosters</link>: Bionic Duplicants gain specialized building usage and increase attributes by installing boosters. These can be added or removed at any time to customize a Bionic Duplicant's career path or mitigate the consequences of bionic bugs.\n\n<link=\"ROLES\">Skills</link>: Performing colony duties helps Bionic Duplicants earn skill points that can be exchanged for skills that may increase attributes and expand their capacity to install <link=\"BOOSTER\">Boosters</link> and <link=\"ELECTROBANK\">Power Banks</link>.\n\n<link=\"MORALE\">Morale</link>: Morale in excess of a Duplicant's expectations will trigger Overjoyed responses that positively affect a variety of colony functions. <link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSRECBUILDING\">Recreational</link> building usage, <link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSDECORATION\">attractive buildings </link> that increase <link=\"DECOR\">Decor</link>, and improved <link=\"FOOD\">Foods</link> contribute to higher morale.\n\n<link=\"STRESS\">Stress</link>: When Stress levels reach 100%, Bionic Duplicants will exhibit negative Stress responses that can disrupt work and damage buildings.\n\n<link=\"TECH\">Research</link>: Using <link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSSCIENCEBUILDING\">science buildings</link> unlocks advanced technologies that increase work efficiency and improve the colony's standard of living.\n\n<i>More information about sustaining Bionic Duplicants' well-being is covered in <link=\"MISCELLANEOUSTIPS\">Tips</link> and <link=\"LESSONS\">Tutorials</link>.</i>\n\n"
msgstr "<link=\"BOOSTER\">增效卡匣</link>：仿生複製人透過安裝增效卡匣獲得專門的建築使用權並增加屬性。可以隨時添加或刪除這些內容，以客製化仿生複製人的職涯道路或減輕仿生錯誤造成的後果。\n\n<link=\"ROLES\">技能</link>：執行殖民地職責可幫助仿生複製人獲得技能點，這些技能點可兌換為可增加屬性並擴展其安裝<link=\"BOOSTER\">增效卡匣</link>和<link=\"ELECTROBANK\">行動電源</link>的能力。\n\n<link=\"MORALE\">士氣</link>：超過複製人期望的士氣會觸發樂歪反應，從而對各種殖民地功能產生正面影響。使用<link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSRECBUILDING\">娛樂</link>建築、增加<link=\"DECOR\">裝飾</link>的<link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSDECORATION\">美觀建築</link>，以及改良的<link=\"FOOD\">食物</link>都有助於提高士氣。\n\n<link=\"STRESS\">壓力</link>：當壓力達到 100% 時，仿生複製人將表現出負面的壓力反應，可能會擾亂工作並損壞建築物。\n\n<link=\"TECH\">研究</link>：使用<link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSSCIENCEBUILDING\">科學建築</link>可以解鎖先進技術，從而提高工作效率並改善殖民地的生活水準。\n\n<i>有關如何維持仿生複製人福祉的更多資訊，請參閱<link=\"MISCELLANEOUSTIPS\">提示</link>和<link=\"LESSONS\">教學課程</link>。</i>\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Specialized Colony Worker"
msgstr "專門的殖民地工人"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.TITLE"
msgid "Bionic Duplicant"
msgstr "仿生複製人"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Boosters are programming modules designed to improve and expand Bionic Duplicants' abilities.\n\nBoosters consume a significant amount of processing power during access and implementation. Bionic Duplicants can expand their capacity for booster installation by accumulating skill points.\n\nBoosters can be combined to grant a broader range of skills, as well as to counteract bionic bugs that may exist in their original programming."
msgstr "增效卡匣是設計用於提高和擴展仿生複製人能力的程式模組。\n\n增效卡匣在存取和實施過程中消耗大量的處理能力。仿生複製人可以透過累積技能點來擴充其安裝增效卡匣的能力。\n\n增效卡匣可以透過組合來提供更廣泛的技能，並抵消原始程式中可能存在的仿生錯誤。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Bionic Systems"
msgstr "仿生系統"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.TITLE"
msgid "Boosters"
msgstr "增效卡匣"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Bliss Burst is a succulent in the genus Haworthia and is a hardy plant well-suited for beginner gardeners.\n\nThey require little in the way of upkeep, to the point that the most common cause of death for Bliss Bursts is overwatering from over-eager carers."
msgstr "天堂草一種十二卷屬的多肉植物，它很強壯，適合初學者種植。\n\n它們幾乎不需要照顧，常見的死因是過度的灌溉。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Decorative Plant"
msgstr "裝飾植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.TITLE"
msgid "Bliss Burst"
msgstr "天堂草"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Alveo Vera's fleshy stems are dotted with small apertures featuring bidirectional valves through which <link=\"CARBONDIOXIDE\">Carbon Dioxide</link> is absorbed and sticky oxygenated waste is secreted.\n\nThe buildup from this respiration cycle crystallizes into <link=\"OXYROCK\">Oxylite</link> ore.\n\nHorticulturists have long been curious about the protective epithelium that prevents the <link=\"OXYROCK\">Oxylite</link> ore from sublimating while on the plant. Unfortunately, it is too fragile to survive handling, and has thus far proven impossible to study."
msgstr "多孔蘆薈的肉質莖上分佈著小孔，這些孔具有雙向閥膜，可以吸收<link=\"CARBONDIOXIDE\">二氧化碳</link>並分泌黏性含氧廢物。\n\n這種呼吸迴圈產生的分泌物最終會結晶成<link=\"OXYROCK\">氧石</link>。\n\n園藝家長期以來都對其保護性的上皮細胞感到好奇，因為這種上皮細胞能防止植物上的<link=\"OXYROCK\">氧石</link>昇華。不幸的是，上皮細胞過於脆弱而無法承受任何方式的處理，因此到目前為止，研究也無法進行。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Plant"
msgstr "植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.TITLE"
msgid "Alveo Vera"
msgstr "多孔蘆薈"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Bluff Briars have formed a symbiotic relationship with a closely related plant strain, the <link=\"PRICKLEFLOWER\">Bristle Blossom</link>.\n\nThey tend to thrive in areas where the Bristle Blossom is present, as the berry it produces emits a rare chemical while decaying that the Briar is capable of absorbing to supplement its own pheromone production."
msgstr "魅惑棘與其相關品種<link=\"PRICKLEFLOWER\">鬃花</link>形成共生關係。\n\n它們常出現在鬃果繁植的區域，因為鬃花會散發一種化學物質，同時魅惑棘能吸收以補充它們的費洛蒙。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "Due to the Bluff Briar's unique pheromonal \"charm\" defense, animals are extremely unlikely to eat it in the wild.\n\nAs a result, the Briar's barbs have become ineffectual over time and are unlikely to cause injury, unlike the Bristle Blossom, which possesses barbs that are exceedingly sharp and require careful handling."
msgstr "由於魅惑棘獨特的費洛蒙「迷惑」的保護，在野外動物極度不喜歡吃它。\n\n結果，隨著時間過去，魅惑棘上的倒刺變得沒什麼殺傷力，不像鬃花它的倒刺非常鋒利需要小心處理。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Decorative Plant"
msgstr "裝飾植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.TITLE"
msgid "Bluff Briar"
msgstr "魅惑棘"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Bog Buckets get their name from their bucket-like flowers and their propensity to grow in swampy, bog-like environments.\n\nThe flower secretes a thick, sweet liquid which collects at the bottom of the bucket and can be gathered for consumption.\n\nThough not inherently dangerous, the interior of the Bog Bucket flower is so warm and inviting that it has tempted individuals to climb inside for a nap, only to awake trapped in its sticky sap."
msgstr "沼澤豬籠草的名字來自於其呈桶狀的花朵以及喜好生長在沼澤環境而得名。\n\n花朵分泌濃稠香甜的汁液，匯集在底部，可供採集食用。\n\n雖然本身並不危險，花朵內部卻溫暖舒適且極具吸引力，常有人受其吸引爬進去小憩，醒來卻發現自己困在黏稠的汁液中。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.TITLE"
msgid "Bog Bucket"
msgstr "沼澤豬籠草"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Bristle Blossom is frequently cultivated for its calorie dense and relatively fast growing Bristle Berries.\n\nConsumption of the berry requires special preparation due to the thick barbs surrounding the edible fruit.\n\nThe term \"Bristle Berry\" is, in fact, a misnomer, as it is not a \"berry\" by botanical definition but an aggregate fruit made up of many smaller fruitlets."
msgstr "鬃花被經常種植，因為它的果實熱量高且生長速度快。\n\n食用鬃果需特殊的工具，因為它的表面有刺。\n\n「鬃果」一詞實際上是一種不正確叫法，因為它不是植物學定義的「漿果」，而是由許多小小果實組成的集合體果實。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.TITLE"
msgid "Bristle Blossom"
msgstr "鬃花"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "As a byproduct of photosynthesis, the Buddy Bud naturally secretes a compound that is chemically similar to the neuropeptide created in the human brain after receiving a hug."
msgstr "作為光合作用的副產品，同心芽會自然分泌一種化學結構近似於人類在擁抱後大腦所產生之神經肽的化合物。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Decorative Plant"
msgstr "裝飾植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.TITLE"
msgid "Buddy Bud"
msgstr "同心芽"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "On a molecular level, it is nearly impossible to distinguish between the Bulbloom's translucent bulbar envelope and high-quality arachnid silk.\n\nThis combination of strength and extensibility keep its bright bloom intact in even the strongest currents, making this plant a beacon of hope in dark marine environments."
msgstr "在分子層面上，幾乎無法區分燈泡花那半透明的球莖外膜與高品質的蛛絲。\n\n其強度與延展性結合的特性，使其即便在強勁的水流中也能保持花朵完好，成為了黑暗海洋環境中的希望之光。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Decor Plant"
msgstr "裝飾植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.TITLE"
msgid "Bulbloom"
msgstr "燈泡花"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Mimikas are difficult to categorize. Biologists theorize that the <link=\"BUTTERFLYPLANT\">Mimika Bud</link> engages in this rare variation of reproductive mimicry to improve seed-dispersal and survive the extinction of key species native to its original habitat.\n\nThese charming moth-like organisms feature a microscopic cluster of phytoprotein \"brain\" cells and are driven by a singular instinct to tend to their host plants.\n\nDue to a monogenic malfunction, however, this plant-tending behavior benefits all of the flora in its area <i>except</i> its own."
msgstr "擬葉蛾難以分類。生物學家推測，<link=\"BUTTERFLYPLANT\">擬葉蛾芽</link>透過這種罕見的生殖擬態變異，來提升種子傳播效率，從而在其原生地一些關鍵物種滅絕後也能得以存活。\n\n這些迷人的類蛾生物體內具有微小的植物蛋白「腦」細胞叢集，受一種奇異本能的驅動，會照料它們的宿主植物。\n\n然而，由於單基因的缺陷，這種照料行為會使區域內<b>自身以外</b>的所有植物受益。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Uncategorized Organism"
msgstr "未分類生物體"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Mimikas"
msgstr "擬蛾類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter?"
msgstr "小動物？"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.TITLE"
msgid "Mimika"
msgstr "擬葉蛾"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLYPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLYPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Mimika Buds are excellent companion plants that provide a farm with the advantages of beneficial insect presence without the challenges of managing an additional critter population.\n\nInside each tightly wrapped bud is a highly concentrated pool of enzymes and imaginal discs similar to those found in the Lepidoptera insect family.\n\nUnder the right conditions, this unique concoction produces a <link=\"BUTTERFLY\">Mimika</link>, an ephemeral pseudo-insect organism that accelerates growth in neighboring plants before settling into its final seed form.\n\nThe sight of a <link=\"BUTTERFLY\">Mimika</link> never fails to fill a gardener with awe."
msgstr "擬葉蛾芽是絕佳的伴生植物，能為農場帶來有益昆蟲的優勢，同時免去管理額外生物群體的挑戰。\n\n每個緊密包裹的芽中都含有高濃度的酶和類似鱗翅目昆蟲的胚盤。\n\n在適宜條件下，這種獨特的混合物將孕育出一隻<link=\"BUTTERFLY\">擬葉蛾</link>，這是一種短暫的類昆蟲生物，在最終化為種子形態之前，能顯著加速周邊植物的生長。\n\n每當<link=\"BUTTERFLY\">擬葉蛾</link>現身，總能令園丁驚嘆不已。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLYPLANT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLYPLANT.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLYPLANT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLYPLANT.TITLE"
msgid "Mimika Bud"
msgstr "擬葉蛾芽"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.C01_EVIL.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.C01_EVIL.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Clearly Nikola is evil. He has some kind of scheme going on that he's keeping secret from the rest of Gravitas and I haven't been able to crack what that is because it's offline and he's always at his computer. Whenever I ask him what he's up to he says I wouldn't understand. Pfft! We both went through the same particle physics classes, buddy. Just because you mash a keyboard and I adjust knobs does not mean I don't know what the Time Containment Field does.\n\nAnd then today I dropped a wrench and Nikola nearly jumped out of his skin! He spun around and screamed at me never to do that again. And then when I said, \"Geez, it's not the end of the world,\" he was like, \"Yeah, it's not like the world will blow up if I get this wrong\" really sarcastic-like.\n\nWhich technically is true. If the Time Containment Field were to break down, the Temporal Bow could theoretically blow up the world. But that's why there are safety systems in place. And safety systems on safety systems. And then safety systems on top of that. But then again he built all the safety systems, so if he wanted to...\n------------------\n"
msgstr "顯然 Nikola 是邪惡的。他正在進行某種計劃，需要對引力科技的其它成員保密，我無法弄清楚是什麼，因為他總是在他的電腦旁，且他的電腦處於離線狀態。每當我問他在做什麼時，他都會說我聽不懂。嘖！我們都上過相同的粒子物理課，哥們。僅因為你組合了鍵盤而我調整旋鈕，並不意味著我不知道「時間限制」的作用。\n\n然後今天我丟了一個扳手，Nikola 嚇了一跳！他轉過身來並向我大叫，別再這樣做了。然後當我說：「天啊，這不是世界末日」時，他說：「是啊，就算我把這個弄錯了，世界似乎也不會因此崩潰了」 真是諷刺。\n\n但就技術上來說是對的。如果打破時間力場，時光之弓可能會毀了世界，這就是為什麼需要安全系統的原因。以及第二層的安全系統，最後是最上層安全系統。但所有的安全系統都是他建立的，因此如果他想…\n------------------\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.C01_EVIL.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.C01_EVIL.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "I decided to get into work early today but when I got in Nikola was already there and it looked like he hadn't been home all weekend. He was pacing back and forth in the lab, monologuing but not like an evil villain. Like someone who hadn't slept in a week.\n\n\"Ruby,\" he said. \"You have to promise me that if anything goes wrong you'll turn on this machine. They're pushing it too far. The printing pods are pushing the...It's too much - TOO MUCH! Something's going to blow. I tried... I'm trying to save it. Not the Earth. There's no hope for the Earth, it's all going to...\" then he made this exploding sound. \"But the Universe. Time itself. It could all go, don't you see? This machine can contain it. Put a Temporal Containment Field around the Earth so time itself doesn't break down and...and...\"\n\nThen all of a sudden these security guys came in. New guys. People I haven't seen before. And they just took him away. Then they took me to a room and asked me all kinds of questions and I answered them, I guess. I don't remember much because the whole time I was thinking - What if I was wrong? What if he's not evil, but Gravitas is?\n\nWhat if I was wrong and what if he's right?\n------------------\n"
msgstr "我決定今天早點上班，但當我到了時 Nikola 已經在那了，看上去他整個周末都沒回家。\n\n他在實驗室來回走動，自言自語，但不像是中邪。倒像是一整個星期都沒睡覺的人。\n\n「Ruby」，他說。「你必須答應我，如果出了甚麼問題，你就打開這台機器。他們推得太過極限了。列印元已經極限…太多了－太多了！有甚麼東西就要炸開了。我試過了…我嘗試著拯救它。不是地球。地球早已經沒有希望，一切都將…」然後他吼了起來。「是宇宙。時間本身。一切都完了，你不明白嗎？這台機器可以制止它。它能在地球周圍放個時間力場，這樣時間本身就不會崩潰，然後…然後…」\n\n然後突然間保全人員都來了。一些新的傢伙。是我以前從沒見過的。接著他們將他帶走了。然後他們會將我帶到一個房間，還問了我各種問題，我都回答了他們，大概吧。我記不清了，因為我一直在想－－如果我是錯的呢？如果他不是邪惡的，但引力科技是呢？\n\n如果我是錯的，而他是對的怎麼辦？\n------------------\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.C01_EVIL.BODY.CONTAINER3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.C01_EVIL.BODY.CONTAINER3"
msgid "No seriously - what if he's right?\n------------------\n"
msgstr "認真－萬一他是對的？\n------------------\n"

