#. STRINGS.CODEX.C7_FIRSTCOLONY.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.C7_FIRSTCOLONY.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The first experiments with establishing a colony off planet were an unmitigated disaster. Without outside help, our current Artificial Intelligence was completely incapable of making the kind of spontaneous decisions needed to deal with unforeseen circumstances. Additionally, the colony subjects lacked the forethought to even build themselves toilet facilities, even after soiling themselves repeatedly.\n\nWhile initial experiments in a lab setting were encouraging, our latest operation on non-Terra soil revealed some massive inadequacies to our system. If this idea is ever going to work, we will either need to drastically improve the AI directing the subjects, or improve the brains of our Duplicants to the point where they possess higher cognitive functions.\n\nGiven the disastrous complications that I could foresee arising if our Duplicants were made less supplicant, I'm leaning toward a push to improve our Artificial Intelligence.\n\nMeanwhile, we will have to send a clean-up crew to destroy all evidence of our little experiment beneath the Ceres' surface. We can't risk anyone discovering the remnants of our failed colony, even if that's unlikely to happen for another few decades at least.\n\n(Sometimes it boggles my mind how much further behind Gravitas the rest of the world is.)"
msgstr "第一次在外星建立殖民地的實驗，是一場十足的災難。沒有外部的幫助，我們目前的人工智慧完全無法應對那些不可預知的情況。此外，殖民地實驗體即使在反複地弄髒自己後，也缺少為自己建造廁所的先見之明。\n\n雖然在實驗室的初步實驗令人鼓舞，但我們在非地球土壤上的最新行動揭示了系統的巨大缺陷。如果這想法行得通，我們將會需要大規模改善指導受試者的 AI，或是強化我們的複製人大腦，來提高他們的認知功能。\n\n考慮到如果讓複製人變得不那麼服從，可能引發的災難性後果，我更傾向於推動 AI 的改進。\n\n同時，我們必須派遣一支清潔隊，摧毀所有埋藏在穀神星地表層下的實驗證據。即使在幾十年內不太可能被發現，我們也不能冒險讓任何人發現失敗殖民的遺跡。\n\n（有時候讓我難以置信，世界的其他地方落後引力科技有多遠。）"

