msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.CRITTERSTATUS_TITLE"
msgid "Field Guide"
msgstr "生物指南"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "All critters are wild when first encountered, with the exception of babies hatched from eggs laid by domesticated adults—those will be born tame.\n\nDuring the domestication process, the critter becomes less self-reliant and develops a higher baseline of expectations regarding its environment and care. Its metabolism accelerates, resulting in an increased level of required calories.\n\nCritters can be domesticated by Duplicants with the Critter Ranching skill at the Grooming Station, and get excited when it's their turn to be fussed over."
msgstr "所有小動物在第一次遇到時都是野生的，但從馴化的成年體產出的蛋孵化出的幼體除外——這些小傢伙生來就是溫順的。\n\n在馴化過程中，這些生物會變得不那麼自力更生，並期望能有更好的環境和照顧。其代謝會加速，導致生存所需的卡路里也增加。\n\n小動物可以被擁有畜牧技能的複製人在梳理站馴化，當輪到被照顧時會很興奮。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TAME.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TAME.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Domesticated critters produce far more resources and lay eggs at a higher frequency than wild ones. They require additional care in order to maintain the levels of happiness that maximize their utility in the colony. (Happy critters are also generally more pleasant to be around.)\n\nGrooming and feeding stations enable Duplicants to domesticate critters."
msgstr "馴化的小動物能比野生小動物產生更多資源，且產蛋頻率更高。牠們需要額外的照料才能維持幸福度，進而在殖民地中發揮最大效益。（快樂的小動物通常也更討人喜歡。）\n\n小動物梳理台與餵食站能讓複製人馴化小動物。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TAME.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TAME.SUBTITLE"
msgid "<b>Effects</b>"
msgstr "<b>效果</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TAME.TAME_HAPPINESS
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TAME.TAME_HAPPINESS"
msgid "    • Happiness\n"
msgstr "    • 幸福度\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TAME.TAME_METABOLISM
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TAME.TAME_METABOLISM"
msgid "    • Critter Metabolism"
msgstr "    • 小動物代謝"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TAME.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TAME.TITLE"
msgid "Tame"
msgstr "溫順"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.TITLE"
msgid "Domestication"
msgstr "馴化"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.WILD.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.WILD.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Wild critters do not require feeding by the colony's Critter Ranchers, thanks to their slower metabolism. They do, however, produce fewer materials than domesticated critters.\n\nApproaching a wild critter to trap or wrangle it is quite safe, provided that it is a non-hostile species. Attacking a critter will typically provoke a combat response."
msgstr "野生小動物不需要殖民地的畜牧員餵食，這都歸因於其緩慢的代謝。然而，牠們要比馴化的小動物產生更少的材料。\n\n只要是沒有敵意的小動物，接近牠並用陷阱捕捉或直接捕捉都是安全的。攻擊小動物通常會引發戰鬥。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.WILD.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.WILD.SUBTITLE"
msgid "<b>Effects</b>"
msgstr "<b>效果</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.WILD.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.WILD.TITLE"
msgid "Wild"
msgstr "野性"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.WILD.WILD_METABOLISM
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.WILD.WILD_METABOLISM"
msgid "    • Critter Metabolism\n"
msgstr "    • 小動物代謝\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.WILD.WILD_POOP
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.DOMESTICATION.WILD.WILD_POOP"
msgid "    • Resource Production\n"
msgstr "    • 資源生產\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Reproductive rates and methods vary among species. The majority lay eggs that must be incubated in order to hatch the next generation of critters.\n\nFactors that influence the rate of reproduction include egg care, happiness, living conditions and domestication."
msgstr "繁殖速率和方式因物種而異。大多數小動物產下的蛋必須孵化才能破殼成為下一代。\n\n影響繁殖速率的因素包括蛋的照料、幸福度、生活條件和馴化。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.EGGCHANCES.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.EGGCHANCES.CONTAINER1"
msgid "In most cases, an egg will hatch into the same critter variant as its parent. Genetic volatility, however, means that there is a chance that it may hatch into another variant from that species.\n\nThere are many things that can alter the likelihood of a critter laying a particular type of egg.\n\nEgg chances are impacted by:\n    • Diet\n    • Body temperature\n    • Ambient gasses and elements\n    • Plants in the critters' care\n    • Variants that share the enclosure\n\nWhen a tame critter lays an egg, the resulting offspring will be born tame."
msgstr "在大多數情況下，蛋會孵化為與其親代相同的小動物變種。然而，遺傳波動性的存在導致其有機率孵化為同一物種的另一種變體。\n\n有許多條件可以改變小動物產特定型別的蛋的機率。產蛋機率受以下因素影響：\n    • 飲食\n    • 體溫\n    • 環境氣體和元素\n    • 小動物照料的植物\n    • 同一房間的變種\n\n當溫順小動物產蛋時，其後代出生時也是溫順的。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.EGGCHANCES.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.EGGCHANCES.TITLE"
msgid "Egg Chances"
msgstr "產蛋機率"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FERTILITYRATE.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FERTILITYRATE.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Each time a critter completes their reproduction cycle (i.e. at 100 percent), it lays an egg and restarts its cycle.\n\nA critter's environment greatly impacts its base reproduction rate. When a critter is feeling cramped, it will wait until all eggs in the room have hatched or been removed before laying any of its own.\n\nCritters will also stop reproducing when they feel confined, which happens when their space is too small or they are stuck in a door or tile.\n\nMood and domestication also impact reproduction: happy critters reproduce more regularly, and happy tame critters reproduce the fastest."
msgstr "小動物在完成其繁殖周期（即100%）時，會產下一顆蛋並重新開始這其周期。\n\n小動物的環境會對其基礎繁殖率產生很大影響。當小動物感到擁擠時，牠會等房間中的所有蛋孵化或被移走後才會產下自己的蛋。\n\n當小動物感覺狹窄時，牠們也會停止繁殖，這種情況會發生在牠們的空間太小或牠們卡在門或磚中時。\n\n心情和馴化也會影響繁殖：快樂的小動物會更定期地繁殖，快樂而溫順的小動物繁殖最快。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FERTILITYRATE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FERTILITYRATE.TITLE"
msgid "Reproduction Rate"
msgstr "繁殖速率"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FUTURE_OVERCROWDED.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FUTURE_OVERCROWDED.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Crowded critters—or critters who know they'll start feeling crowded once all of the eggs in the room have hatched—will temporarily stop laying eggs. Their reproductive system will resume function once all eggs have hatched or been removed from the room."
msgstr "感覺擁擠的小動物——或者那些知道一旦房間裡所有的蛋都孵化出來，就會開始感到擁擠的小動物——會暫時停止產卵。一旦所有蛋孵化或從房間中移出，牠們的生殖系統就會恢復功能。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FUTURE_OVERCROWDED.CRAMPED_FERTILITY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FUTURE_OVERCROWDED.CRAMPED_FERTILITY"
msgid "    • Reproduction"
msgstr "    • 繁殖率"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FUTURE_OVERCROWDED.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FUTURE_OVERCROWDED.SUBTITLE"
msgid "<b>Effects</b>"
msgstr "<b>效果</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FUTURE_OVERCROWDED.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.FUTURE_OVERCROWDED.TITLE"
msgid "Cramped"
msgstr "狹窄"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.INCUBATION.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.INCUBATION.CONTAINER1"
msgid "A critter's incubation time is one-fifth of their total lifetime: for example, if a critter's maximum age is 100 cycles, its egg will take 20 cycles to hatch.\n\nIncubation rates can be accelerated through tender intervention by a Critter Rancher. Lullabied eggs—that is, those that have been sung to—will incubate faster and hatch sooner than eggs that have not received such tender care. Being cuddled by a Cuddle Pip also accelerates the rate of incubation.\n\nEggs can be cuddled anywhere, but can only be lullabied when placed inside an Incubator. The effects of lullabies and cuddles are cumulative."
msgstr "小動物的孵化時間是其總壽命的五分之一：比如，小動物的最大年齡為 100 周期，則該小動物的蛋需要 20 周期孵化。\n\n孵化速率可以透過畜牧員照料而加速。聽過搖籃曲的蛋會比未受照料的蛋更快孵化。被抱抱樹鼠擁抱也會加快孵化。\n\n蛋可以在任何地方被擁抱，但必須置於孵化器中才能對其歌唱。搖籃曲和擁抱的效果是可累加的。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.INCUBATION.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.INCUBATION.TITLE"
msgid "Incubation"
msgstr "孵化度"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.MAXAGE.CONTAINER1_DLC1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.MAXAGE.CONTAINER1_DLC1"
msgid "With the exception of the Beeta Hive and the Morb—which can live indefinitely if left to their own devices—critters have a fixed life expectancy. The maximum age indicates the highest number of cycles that critters will live, barring starvation or other unnatural causes of death.\n\nIf critters are injured or unhealthy, a Critter Rancher can restore their health at the Grooming Station.\n\nBabyhood, the period before a critter is mature enough to reproduce, is marked by a slower metabolism and the easy happiness of youth.\n\nMost species live for 75 to 100 cycles on average. The shortest-lived critter is the Beeta, whose lifespan is only five cycles long."
msgstr "除了輻射蜂巢和莫布——任其自生自滅就會永久存活——小動物都有固定的預期壽命。最大年齡表明了小動物能存活的最大周期數，除了餓死或其他非自然死因。\n\n如果小動物受傷或不健康，則可以讓小動物照服員在梳理站恢復其健康。\n\n幼年期是小動物足夠成熟能繁殖之前的時期，其特點是代謝更慢，更容易保持幸福度。\n\n大多數物種平均壽命為 75 至 100 周期。壽命最短的小動物是輻射蜂，其壽命只有 5 周期。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.MAXAGE.CONTAINER1_VANILLA
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.MAXAGE.CONTAINER1_VANILLA"
msgid "With the exception of the Morb—which can live indefinitely if left to its own devices—critters have a fixed life expectancy. The maximum age indicates the highest number of cycles that critters will live, barring starvation or other unnatural causes of death.\n\nBabyhood, the period before a critter is mature enough to reproduce, is marked by a slower metabolism and the easy happiness of youth.\n\nMost species live for 75 to 100 cycles on average."
msgstr "除了莫布——任其自生自滅就會永久存活——小動物都有固定的預期壽命。最大年齡表明了小動物能存活的最大周期數，除了餓死或其他非自然死因。\n\n幼年期是小動物足夠成熟能繁殖之前的時期，其特點是代謝更慢，更容易保持幸福度。\n\n大多數物種平均壽命為 75 至 100 周期。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.MAXAGE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.MAXAGE.TITLE"
msgid "Max Age"
msgstr "最大年齡"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.FERTILITY.TITLE"
msgid "Reproduction"
msgstr "繁殖度"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "A critter's metabolic rate is a measure of their appetite and the materials that they excrete as a result.\n\nCritters with higher metabolism get hungry more often. Those with lower metabolism will consume less food, but this reduced caloric intake results in fewer resources being produced.\n\nThe digestive process is influenced by conditions such as domestication, mood, and whether the critter in question is a juvenile (baby) or an adult."
msgstr "小動物的代謝速率用於衡量其食慾與其排出材料的快慢。\n\n有著高代謝的小動物會經常飢餓。而低代謝的小動物不容易餓，但攝入量不高會導致其資源產生量也不高。\n\n馴化、心情、是幼體還是成年體等條件都會影響消化過程。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.HUNGRY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.HUNGRY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Tame critters have significantly faster metabolism than wild ones, and get hungry sooner. This makes them more valuable in terms of resource production, as long as the colony is equipped to meet their dietary needs.\n\nCritters' stomachs vary in size, but they are capable of storing at least five cycles' worth of food. Their bellies begin to rumble when those internal caches drop below 90 percent. The critter will then seek out food, and will continue to eat until they feel completely full again.\n\nJuvenile critters have the slowest metabolism, although glum tame critters are not far behind."
msgstr "馴養的動物比野生動物的新陳代謝快得多，而且更容易感到飢餓。這使得它們在資源生產方面更有價值，只要殖民地有能力滿足它們的飲食需求。\n\n小動物的胃容量大小不一，但都能儲存至少 5 周期的食物。當儲量低於 90% 時，牠們的肚子就會開始隆隆作響。然後，小動物會尋找食物，並繼續進食，直到再次感到完全飽為止。\n\n幼體小動物的代謝最慢，儘管悶悶不樂的馴養小動物也緊隨其後。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.HUNGRY.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.HUNGRY.TITLE"
msgid "Hungry"
msgstr "飢餓"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.STARVING.CONTAINER1_DLC1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.STARVING.CONTAINER1_DLC1"
msgid "With the exception of Morbs and Beetas—which require zero calories to survive—tame critters will die after {0} cycles of consistent starvation. Wild critters do not starve to death."
msgstr "除莫布和輻射蜂之外——牠們不需要卡路里就能生存——溫順小動物持續飢餓 {0} 周期後會餓死。野生小動物不會餓死。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.STARVING.CONTAINER1_VANILLA
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.STARVING.CONTAINER1_VANILLA"
msgid "With the exception of Morbs—which require zero calories to survive—tame critters will die after {0} cycles of consistent starvation. Wild critters do not starve to death."
msgstr "除莫布之外——牠不需要卡路里就能生存——溫順小動物持續飢餓 {0} 周期後會餓死。野生小動物不會餓死。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.STARVING.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.STARVING.TITLE"
msgid "Starving"
msgstr "飢餓"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.METABOLISM.TITLE"
msgid "Metabolism"
msgstr "代謝"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "As with many living things, critters are susceptible to fluctuations in mood. While they are incapable of articulating their feelings verbally, these variations have observable effects on productivity and reproduction.\n\nFactors that influence a critter's mood include: grooming, wildness/tameness, habitat, overcrowding, confinement, and Brackene consumption."
msgstr "與許多生物一樣，小動物也容易被心情波動影響。雖然牠們無法直接表達自己的感受，但這些變化會對生產和繁殖有明顯影響。\n\n影響小動物心情的因素包括：飢餓、打扮、野生/溫順、生活環境、過度擁擠、封閉和鹹乳消耗。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.CONFINED.CONFINED_FERTILITY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.CONFINED.CONFINED_FERTILITY"
msgid "    • Reproduction\n"
msgstr "    • 繁殖率\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.CONFINED.CONFINED_HAPPINESS
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.CONFINED.CONFINED_HAPPINESS"
msgid "    • Happiness"
msgstr "    • 幸福度"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.CONFINED.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.CONFINED.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Each species has its own space requirements. Critters who find themselves in a room or pool that they consider too small will feel confined. They will feel the same way if they become stuck in a door or tile. Critters will not reproduce while they are in this state.\n\nShove Voles are the exception to this rule: their tunneling instincts make them quite comfortable in snug spaces, and they never feel confined."
msgstr "每個物種都有其自己的空間需求。如果小動物發現自己身處在太小的房間或水池中，就會感覺到狹窄。若牠們卡在門或方塊磚中，也會有相同的感受。小動物在這種狀態下將無法繁殖。\n\n鑽地田鼠是這個規則的例外：牠們的挖掘本能讓牠們在狹窄空間中相當怡然自得，且永遠不會感覺到狹窄。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.CONFINED.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.CONFINED.SUBTITLE"
msgid "<b>Effects</b>"
msgstr "<b>效果</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.CONFINED.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.CONFINED.TITLE"
msgid "Confined"
msgstr "狹窄"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.GLUM.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.GLUM.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Critters can survive in subpar environments, but it takes a toll on their mood and impacts metabolism and productivity. When their happiness levels dip below zero, they become glum.\n\nWild critters are less sensitive to the effects of glumness than their tamed brethren, though they are still negatively affected by crowded or confined living conditions."
msgstr "小動物可以在惡劣的環境中生存，但這會影響牠們的情緒並影響新陳代謝和生產力。當牠們的幸福水平降至 0 以下時，它們就會變得悶悶不樂。\n\n\n\n野生動物對悶悶不樂的影響不如牠們被馴服的同胞那麼敏感，儘管牠們仍然受到擁擠或狹窄的生活條件的負面影響。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.GLUM.GLUMWILD_METABOLISM
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.GLUM.GLUMWILD_METABOLISM"
msgid "    • Critter Metabolism\n"
msgstr "    • 小動物代謝\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.GLUM.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.GLUM.SUBTITLE"
msgid "<b>Effects</b>"
msgstr "<b>效果</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.GLUM.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.GLUM.TITLE"
msgid "Glum"
msgstr "悶悶不樂"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HAPPY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HAPPY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Happy, tame critters produce more usable materials and tend to lay eggs at a higher rate than glum or wild critters. Domesticated critters are less resilient than wild ones—they require more care from the colony in order to maintain a positive disposition.\n\nBabies have a higher baseline of natural joy, but produce neither resources nor eggs.\n\nDuplicants with the Critter Ranching skill have the expertise needed to domesticate and care for critters. They can boost a critter's mood and tend to their health at a Grooming Station.\n\nCritters who drink at the Critter Fountain also enjoy a mood boost, despite the lack of nutrients available in the Brackene dispensed.\n\nBeing confined or feeling crowded undermines a critter's happiness."
msgstr "快樂、溫順的生物​​會比憂鬱或野生的生物產生更多可用的材料，並且產蛋速率更快。馴化的小動物適應力不如野生小動物——牠們需要更多來自殖民地的關照才能保持積極的性情。\n\n幼體的幸福度基準更高，但既不產生資源，也不產蛋。\n\n擁有畜牧技能的複製人具有馴化和照料小動物的專業知識，可以在梳理站與小動物建立親密關係而提高小動物的心情。\n\n喝過小動物飲水機的小動物也會享受到心情加成，儘管鹹乳中缺乏有用的營養成分。\n\n被限制或感到擁擠會破壞小動物的幸福感。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HAPPY.HAPPY_METABOLISM
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HAPPY.HAPPY_METABOLISM"
msgid "    • Indirectly improves egg-laying rates"
msgstr "    • 間接提高產蛋率"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HAPPY.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HAPPY.SUBTITLE"
msgid "<b>Effects</b>"
msgstr "<b>效果</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HAPPY.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HAPPY.TITLE"
msgid "Happy"
msgstr "快樂"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HOSTILE.CONTAINER1_DLC1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HOSTILE.CONTAINER1_DLC1"
msgid "Most critters are non-hostile. They may attempt to defend themselves when attacked by Duplicants, though their natural passivity limits the damage caused in these instances.\n\nSome critters, however, have exceptionally strong self-preservation instincts and must be approached with extreme caution. Pokeshells, for example, are not naturally hostile but are fiercely protective of their young and will attack if a Duplicant or critter wanders too close to their eggs.\n\nThe Beeta, on the other hand, is both hostile and radioactive. While it cannot be tamed, it can be subdued through the use of CO2."
msgstr "大多數小動物都是沒有敵意的。牠們在被複製人攻擊時會嘗試保護自己，但其被動天性導致了其傷害不高。\n\n然而，有一些小動物有著異常強烈的自我保護本能，接近時必須格外小心。比如拋殼蟹，雖然天性沒有敵意，但保護其幼體的態度十分強硬，複製人或小動物如果過於靠近拋殼蟹的蛋就會被攻擊。\n\n另一方面，輻射蜂既有敵意又有放射性。雖然不能被馴化，但可以透過使用二氧化碳壓制。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HOSTILE.CONTAINER1_VANILLA
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HOSTILE.CONTAINER1_VANILLA"
msgid "Most critters are non-hostile. They may attempt to defend themselves when attacked by Duplicants, though their natural passivity limits the damage caused in these instances.\n\nSome critters, however, have exceptionally strong self-preservation instincts and must be approached with extreme caution.\n\nPokeshells, for example, are not naturally hostile but are fiercely protective of their young and will attack if a Duplicant or critter wanders too close to their eggs."
msgstr "大多數小動物都是沒有敵意的。牠們在被複製人攻擊時會嘗試保護自己，但其被動天性導致了其傷害不高。\n\n然而，有一些小動物有著異常強烈的自我保護本能，接近時必須格外小心。\n\n比如拋殼蟹，雖然天性沒有敵意，但保護其幼體的態度十分強硬，複製人或小動物如果過於靠近拋殼蟹的蛋就會被攻擊。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HOSTILE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.HOSTILE.TITLE"
msgid "Hostile"
msgstr "敵意"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.MISERABLE.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.MISERABLE.CONTAINER1"
msgid "When too many unpleasant conditions add up, critters become utterly miserable. This level of unhappiness seriously undermines their ability to contribute to the colony. Miserable critters have lower metabolism and will not lay eggs."
msgstr "當太多不愉快的情況加起來時，小動物就會變得非常痛苦。這種程度的不滿嚴重削弱了牠們為殖民地做出貢獻的能力。痛苦的動物新陳代謝較低，不會產卵。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.MISERABLE.MISERABLEWILD_FERTILITY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.MISERABLE.MISERABLEWILD_FERTILITY"
msgid "    • Reproduction"
msgstr "    • 繁殖率"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.MISERABLE.MISERABLEWILD_METABOLISM
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.MISERABLE.MISERABLEWILD_METABOLISM"
msgid "    • Critter Metabolism"
msgstr "    • 小動物新陳代謝"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.MISERABLE.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.MISERABLE.SUBTITLE"
msgid "<b>Effects</b>"
msgstr "<b>效果</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.MISERABLE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.MISERABLE.TITLE"
msgid "Miserable"
msgstr "悲慘"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.NEUTRAL.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.NEUTRAL.CONTAINER1"
msgid "When a critter has no reason to object to anything in its environment or diet, it will feel quite content with its lot in life. Satisfied critters have the default metabolism, fertility and life span expected of their species."
msgstr "當小動物沒有理由反對其環境或飲食中的任何事物時，牠就會對自己的生活感到非常滿意。滿意的生物具有其物種預期的預設新陳代謝、生育力和壽命。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.NEUTRAL.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.NEUTRAL.TITLE"
msgid "Satisfied"
msgstr "滿足"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.OVERCROWDED.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.OVERCROWDED.CONTAINER1"
msgid "This occurs when a critter is in a room or pool that's appropriately sized for its needs but feels that there are too many other critters sharing the same space. Because each species has its own space requirements, this state can vary among occupants of the same room.\n\nThis emotional state intensifies in response to the number of excess critters: adding new critters to an already crowded room will undermine a critter's happiness even further."
msgstr "當小動物身處的房間或水池大小符合其需求，但覺得有太多其他小動物共享同一個空間時，就會進入這種狀態。由於每個物種都有各自的空間需求，因此同一間房內不同個體的感受可能會有所不同。\n\n這種情緒狀態會隨著過剩的小動物數量而加劇：在已經擁擠的房間中加入更多小動物，會進一步降低牠們的快樂度。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.OVERCROWDED.OVERCROWDED_HAPPY1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.OVERCROWDED.OVERCROWDED_HAPPY1"
msgid "    • Happiness\n"
msgstr "    • 幸福度\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.OVERCROWDED.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.OVERCROWDED.SUBTITLE"
msgid "<b>Effects</b>"
msgstr "<b>效果</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.OVERCROWDED.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.OVERCROWDED.TITLE"
msgid "Crowded"
msgstr "擁擠"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRITTERSTATUS.MOOD.TITLE"
msgid "Mood"
msgstr "心情"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRYOTANKWARNINGS.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRYOTANKWARNINGS.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "    • Do not leave the contents of the Cryotank 3000 unattended unless an apocalyptic disaster has left you no choice.\n\n    • Ensure that the Cryotank 3000 has enough battery power to remain active for at least 6000 years.\n\n    • Do not attempt to defrost the contents of the Cryotank 3000 while it is submerged in molten hot lava.\n\n    • Use only a qualified Gravitas Cryotank repair facility to repair your Cryotank 3000. Attempting to service the device yourself will void the warranty.\n\n    • Do not put food in the Cryotank 3000. The Cryotank 3000 is not a refrigerator.\n\n    • Do not allow children to play in the Cryotank 3000. The Cryotank 3000 is not a toy.\n\n    • While the Cryotank 3000 is able to withstand a nuclear blast, Gravitas and its subsidiaries are not responsible for what may happen in the resulting nuclear fallout.\n\n    • Wait at least 5 minutes after being unfrozen from the Cryotank 3000 before operating heavy machinery.\n\n    • Each Cryotank 3000 is good for only one use.\n\n"
msgstr "    • 除非在末日疾病下別無選擇，否則別在無人值守的情形下成為低溫艙 3000 的內容物。\n\n    • 確保低溫艙 3000 最少有可運作 6000 年的剩餘電量。\n\n    • 當低溫艙被熔岩淹沒時不要解凍內容物。\n\n    • 僅使用合格的引力科技低溫艙保養廠來維修你的低溫艙。自行修理將沒有保固。\n\n    • 請勿將食物放進低溫艙 3000。它不是冰箱。\n\n    • 請勿讓小孩在低溫艙 3000 內遊玩。它不是玩具。\n\n    • 雖然低溫艙 3000 能承受核爆，引力科技與其子公司對可能由其產生核輻射概不負責。\n\n    • 從低溫艙 3000 解凍後最少等待 5 分鐘後才能操作重型機械。\n\n    • 每個低溫艙 3000 僅適合一人使用。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRYOTANKWARNINGS.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRYOTANKWARNINGS.SUBTITLE"
msgid "IMPORTANT OPERATING INSTRUCTIONS FOR THE CRYOTANK 3000"
msgstr "低溫艙 3000 的重要操作說明"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRYOTANKWARNINGS.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRYOTANKWARNINGS.TITLE"
msgid "CRYOTANK SAFETY"
msgstr "低溫艙安全"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRYSTAL.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRYSTAL.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Pictured: \"Radiant\" Shine Bug variant</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>圖為：「水晶」 發光蟲變種</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRYSTAL.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRYSTAL.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Morph"
msgstr "小動物變種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.CRYSTAL.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.CRYSTAL.TITLE"
msgid "Radiant Bug"
msgstr "水晶發光蟲"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DASHASALTVINE.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DASHASALTVINE.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Dasha Saltvine is a unique plant that needs large amounts of salt to balance the levels of water in its body.\n\nIn order to keep a supply of salt on hand, the end of the vine is coated in microscopic formations which bind with sodium atoms, forming large crystals over time."
msgstr "沙鹽藤是一種獨特的植物，需要大量的鹽來平衡身體中的水份。\n\n為了維持鹽份補給，藤蔓的末端有著能與鈉原子結合的微型構造，隨著時間經過會形成大型結晶物。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DASHASALTVINE.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DASHASALTVINE.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Spice Plant"
msgstr "食用香料"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DASHASALTVINE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DASHASALTVINE.TITLE"
msgid "Dasha Saltvine"
msgstr "沙鹽藤蔓"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DATABANK.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DATABANK.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Data Banks are a form of portable storage media. They are prized for their non-volatility, robustness, and practical research applications.\n\nThey are not foldable."
msgstr "資料磁片是一種行動式儲存媒體。它們因其非揮發性、穩健性和實際研究應用而備受讚譽。\n\n磁碟不可摺疊。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DATABANK.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DATABANK.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Information Technology"
msgstr "資訊科技"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DATABANK.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DATABANK.TITLE"
msgid "Data Banks"
msgstr "資料磁片"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DECOR.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DECOR.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Pictured: \"Longhair\" Slickster variant</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>圖為：「長髮」小油怪變種</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DECOR.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DECOR.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "Positioned on either side of the Major Rhinophores are Minor Rhinophores, which specialize in mechanical reception and detect air pressure around the Slickster. These send signals to the brain to contract or expand its air sacks accordingly."
msgstr "主要的觸鬚位於次要的觸鬚兩側，是專門用來接收與偵測小油怪周圍的氣壓的器官。這些訊號發送到大腦，於是它的氣囊會收縮或擴張。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DECOR.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DECOR.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Morph"
msgstr "小動物變種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DECOR.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DECOR.TITLE"
msgid "Longhair Slickster"
msgstr "長髮小油怪"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.HEADER_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.HEADER_1"
msgid "Decor"
msgstr "裝飾"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.HEADER_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.HEADER_2"
msgid "Calculating Decor"
msgstr "裝飾計算中"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.HEADER_3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.HEADER_3"
msgid "Tutorials"
msgstr "教學"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.PARAGRAPH_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.PARAGRAPH_1"
msgid "Low Decor can increase Duplicant <link=\"STRESS\">Stress</link>. Thankfully, pretty things tend to increase the Decor value of an area. Each Duplicant has a different idea of what is a high enough Decor value. If the average Decor that a Duplicant experiences in a cycle is below their expectations, they will suffer a stress penalty.\n\n"
msgstr "低裝飾會增加複製人的<link=\"STRESS\">壓力</link>。值得慶幸的是，漂亮的事物往往會增加區域的裝飾值。每位複製人對高裝飾值的看法都不同。如果一周期內複製人感受到的平均裝飾低於他們的期望，那他們將會產生壓力。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.PARAGRAPH_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.PARAGRAPH_2"
msgid "Many things have an effect on the Decor value of a tile. A building's effect is expressed as a strength value and a radius. Often that effect is positive, but many buildings also lower the decor value of an area too. <link=\"PLANTS\">Plants</link>, <link=\"CREATURES\">Critters</link>, and <link=\"BUILDCATEGORYFURNITURE\">Furniture</link> often increase decor while industrial buildings, debris, and rot often decrease it. Duplicants experience the combined decor of all objects affecting a tile.\n\nThe <link=\"PRICKLEGRASS\">Bluff Briar</link> has a decor value of 25 and a radius of 4 tiles. \nThe <link=\"MICROBEMUSHER\">Microbe Musher</link> has a decor value of -15 and a radius of 3 tiles. \nThe result of placing a <link=\"MICROBEMUSHER\">Microbe Musher</link> next to a <link=\"PRICKLEGRASS\">Bluff Briar</link> would be a combined decor value of 10.\n\n"
msgstr "許多事物都會對格子的裝飾值產生影響。建築物的影響以強度值和範圍來表示。通常這個影響是正向的，但許多建築也會降低該區域的裝飾值。<link=\"PLANTS\">植物</link>、<link=\"CREATURES\">動物</link>與<link=\"BUILDCATEGORYFURNITURE\">家具</link>通常會增加裝飾，而工業建築、掉落物與腐壞物通常會減少裝飾。複製人的感受是格子內所有物件效果的總和。\n\n<link=\"PRICKLEGRASS\">魅惑棘</link>的裝飾值 25，影響範圍 4 格。\n<link=\"MICROBEMUSHER\">食物壓製器</link> 的裝飾值 -15，影響範圍 3 格。\n如果<link=\"MICROBEMUSHER\">食物壓製器</link>旁，擺放著<link=\"PRICKLEGRASS\">魅惑棘</link>，那麼最後的裝飾值總和為 10 的裝飾值。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.PARAGRAPH_3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.PARAGRAPH_3"
msgid "To learn more, watch <link=\"VIDEOS13\">Video: Duplicant Morale</link> and see <link=\"MISCELLANEOUSTIPS2\">Tutorial: Stress Management</link>.\n\n"
msgstr "若要了解更多，請觀看<link=\"VIDEOS13\">影片：複製人士氣</link> 並查看<link=\"MISCELLANEOUSTIPS2\">教學：壓力管理</link>。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DECORSYSTEM.TITLE"
msgid "<link=\"DECOR\">Decor</link>"
msgstr "<link=\"DECOR\">裝飾</link>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEERSPECIES.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEERSPECIES.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Evenly distributed throughout the Flox's dense overcoat are countless vibrissae-like hairs that transmit detailed sensory information about its environment, allowing it to detect changes as subtle as the shift in another creature's mood.\n\nFloxes avoid overstimulation by whipping their tails to release the pent-up energy. Because these tactile hairs are so sensitive, they cannot be safely shorn.\n\nFlox antlers, however, are nerveless and cumbersome. Handlers who unburden them of this cranial load are often rewarded with the critter's long, slow blinks of contentment."
msgstr "狐鹿克斯的濃密外層毛均勻分佈著無數觸鬚般的毛髮，能夠傳遞關於環境的感官資訊，\n\n狐鹿克斯透過甩尾巴來釋放積壓的能量以避免過度刺激。由於這些觸覺毛髮非常敏感，所以不能安全地剪掉。\n\n然而，狐鹿克斯角沒有神經連線並且很笨重。幫忙卸下頭角負擔的飼養員常常能獲得這種小動物因滿足而長久而緩慢的眨眼作為獎勵。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEERSPECIES.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEERSPECIES.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Species"
msgstr "小動物物種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEERSPECIES.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEERSPECIES.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Floxes"
msgstr "霜鹿狐類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEERSPECIES.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEERSPECIES.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Domesticable Critter"
msgstr "可馴養的小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEERSPECIES.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEERSPECIES.TITLE"
msgid "Flox"
msgstr "狐鹿克斯"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DENSE.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DENSE.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Pictured: \"Dense\" Puft variant</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>圖為：「氧氣」帕夫變種</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DENSE.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DENSE.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "The Puft is an easy creature to raise for first time handlers given its wholly amiable disposition and suggestible nature.\n\nIt is unusually tolerant of human handling and will allow itself to be patted or scratched nearly anywhere on its fuzzy body, including, unnervingly, directly on any of its three eyeballs."
msgstr "帕夫對初次接觸的人來說，是一種平易近人的動物。\n\n牠非常容易接受人類輕拍或觸碰幾乎牠們身上的任何地方，包括直接觸碰牠們令人不安的三個眼睛。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DENSE.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DENSE.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Morph"
msgstr "小動物變種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DENSE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DENSE.TITLE"
msgid "Dense Puft"
msgstr "氧氣帕夫"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIP.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIP.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "A crystallized blob of <link=\"MILK\">Brackene</link> from the <link=\"DEWDRIPPERPLANT\">Dew Dripper</link>.\n\nIt must be processed at the <link=\"MILKPRESS\">Plant Pulverizer</link> to release its contents."
msgstr "來自<link=\"DEWDRIPPERPLANT\">凝露藤</link>的一團結晶狀<link=\"MILK\">鹹乳</link>。\n\n必須在<link=\"MILKPRESS\">植物粉碎機</link>進行加工才能釋放其內容物。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIP.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIP.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Plant Byproduct"
msgstr "植物副產品"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIP.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIP.TITLE"
msgid "Dewdrip"
msgstr "凝露珠"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIPPERPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIPPERPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Dew Dripper is sometimes referred to as the \"purple starling\" of the plant world for the magnificent feather-like leaves that encircle its base.\n\nThis sculptural plant slow-drips excess sap that coagulates upon contact with air. The resulting globule is so dense that its weight would snap the Dew Dripper's hollow stem if planted in the ground.\n\nNo one has ever been seriously injured by a falling Dewdrip, but it's best not to linger beneath them."
msgstr "凝露藤根部環繞著華麗的羽毛狀葉子，有時被稱為植物界的「紫椋鳥」。\n\n這種雕塑般的植物會緩慢滴下多餘的樹液，樹液接觸空氣後便會凝固。形成的凝結物極其緻密，若種植在地面上，其重量會折斷凝露草的空心莖。\n\n從未有人被掉落的凝露珠嚴重傷害，但最好不要在其下方逗留。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIPPERPLANT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIPPERPLANT.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Cultivable Plant"
msgstr "可耕種植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIPPERPLANT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEWDRIPPERPLANT.TITLE"
msgid "Dew Dripper"
msgstr "凝露藤"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEWPALM.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEWPALM.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Gum Palms have developed an eye-catching defense mechanism similar to that of poisonous amphibians.\n\nBright reddish coloring displayed in their leaves and sharp ornamental bark scales deter most predators, who recognize the warning signs of toxicity. <link=\"PACU\">Pacus</link>, however, consider the tree's highly toxic seed a spicy treat."
msgstr "黏膠棕櫚已經演化出了一種類似有毒兩棲動物的醒目防禦機制。\n\n葉片上鮮豔的紅色與樹皮上鋒利的觀賞性鱗片，能讓大多數捕食者望而卻步，因為牠們能辨識出這些有毒的警告訊號。然而，<link=\"PACU\">帕庫</link>卻將這種樹的劇毒種子視為辛辣的美味。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEWPALM.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEWPALM.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Cultivable Plant"
msgstr "可耕種植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DEWPALM.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DEWPALM.TITLE"
msgid "Gum Palm"
msgstr "黏膠棕櫚"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DIESELMOO.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DIESELMOO.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Pictured: \"Husky\" Moo variant</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>圖為：「絨毛」瓦斯牛變種</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DIESELMOO.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DIESELMOO.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Morph"
msgstr "小動物變異種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DIESELMOO.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DIESELMOO.TITLE"
msgid "Husky Moo"
msgstr "哈烯奇牛"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DINOFERN.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DINOFERN.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<i>Megafrondia Byronalis</i>, commonly known as \"Megafrond,\" is a gigantic plant that dwarfs its surroundings.\n\nIts size is not the only daunting factor in its cultivation: the Megafrond's gigantism is possible thanks to its singular adaptation to cold temperatures and a caustic gas environment that few other living things (including farmers) enjoy.\n\nThese challenges are considered a fair price for bragging rights and a useful grain harvest."
msgstr "<i>拜倫利斯巨型葉狀體 (Megafrondia Byronalis)</i>，俗稱「巨蕨」，是一種使周圍環境相形見絀的巨型植物。\n\n其栽培的困難之處不僅在於體型：巨蕨的巨型化得益於其對低溫和腐蝕性氣體環境的獨特適應，這兩種環境是鮮少其他生物（包括農民）所能忍受的。\n\n這些挑戰被認為是值得付出的代價，既能獲得炫耀的資本，也能帶來有用的穀物收成。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DINOFERN.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DINOFERN.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Cultivable Plant"
msgstr "可耕種植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DINOFERN.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DINOFERN.TITLE"
msgid "Megafrond"
msgstr "巨蕨"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DIVERGENT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DIVERGENT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "'Divergent' is the name given to the two different genders of one species, the Sweetle and the Grubgrub, both of which are able to reproduce asexually and tend to Grubfruit Plants.\n\nWhen tending to the Grubfruit Plant, both gender variants of the Divergent display the exact same behaviors, however the Grubgrub possesses slightly more tiny facial hair which helps in pollinating the plants and stimulates faster growth."
msgstr "「變異蟲」是一個物種名稱，其擁有兩種不同性別，甜素甲蟲與蟲果果蟲，兩者都能無性生殖與照顧蟲蜜草。\n\n當照顧蟲蜜草時兩個變種都展現出相同的行為，然而蟲果果蟲面部的毛髮更細一些，這有助於植物授粉並刺激更快的生長。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DIVERGENT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DIVERGENT.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Domesticable Critter"
msgstr "可馴養的小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DIVERGENT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DIVERGENT.TITLE"
msgid "Divergent"
msgstr "變異蟲"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Dreckos are a reptilian species boasting billions of microscopic hairs on their feet, allowing them to stick to and climb most surfaces."
msgstr "龍鱗蜥是種爬行動物，腳上有數億個微小的絨毛，讓牠們可以附著並攀爬在大多數的表面上。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "The tail of the Drecko, called the \"train\", is purely for decoration and can be lost or shorn without harm to the animal.\n\nAs a result, Drecko fibers are often farmed for use in textile production.\n\nCaring for Dreckos is a fulfilling endeavor thanks to their companionable personalities.\n\nSome domestic Dreckos have even been known to respond to their own names."
msgstr "龍鱗蜥的尾巴叫做「火車」，純粹是為了裝飾，可以捨棄或修剪而不會傷害動物。\n\n因此，人們常常養殖龍鱗蜥，收集其絨毛用於製造紡織物。\n\n由於龍鱗蜥友善的性格，照顧龍鱗蜥是一件很有成就感的事情。\n\n一些馴養的龍鱗蜥在聽到叫自己的名字時甚至會做出反應。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Species"
msgstr "動物類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Dreckos"
msgstr "鱗蜥類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Domesticable Critter"
msgstr "可馴養的小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DRECKO.TITLE"
msgid "Drecko"
msgstr "龍鱗蜥"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DUPLICANT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DUPLICANT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Duplicants are printed at the <link=\"HEADQUARTERS\">Printing Pod</link>, emerging fully formed and clothed in standard-issue uniforms. Unique outfits can be found in the Supply Closet.\n"
msgstr "從<link=\"HEADQUARTERS\">列印元</link>中列印出來的複製人，完全成型並穿著標準制服。可以在供應櫃中找到獨特的外觀。\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DUPLICANT.CODEXCATEGORYNAME
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DUPLICANT.CODEXCATEGORYNAME"
msgid "Duplicants"
msgstr "複製人"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DUPLICANT.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DUPLICANT.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Colony Workers"
msgstr "殖民地工人"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DUPLICANT.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DUPLICANT.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Duplicant Types"
msgstr "複製人類型"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DUSKCAP.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DUSKCAP.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Like many species of mushroom, Dusk Caps thrive in dark areas otherwise ill-suited to the cultivation of plants.\n\nIn place of typical chlorophyll, the underside of a Dusk Cap is fitted with thousands of specialized gills, which it uses to draw in carbon dioxide and aid in its growth."
msgstr "像許多其它種類的蘑菇一樣，黃昏蘑菇生長在黑暗區域，其它地方不適合種植。\n\n取代葉綠素，黃昏蘑菇的傘帽下有成千上萬個毛細孔，用來吸收二氧化碳幫助其生長。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DUSKCAP.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DUSKCAP.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.DUSKCAP.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.DUSKCAP.TITLE"
msgid "Dusk Cap"
msgstr "黃昏蘑菇"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EGG_SHELL.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EGG_SHELL.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The shards left over from the protective walls of a baby critter's first home."
msgstr "小動物第一個家的防護牆留下的碎片。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EGG_SHELL.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EGG_SHELL.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Byproduct"
msgstr "小動物副產品"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EGG_SHELL.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EGG_SHELL.TITLE"
msgid "Egg Shell"
msgstr "蛋殼"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ELECTROBANK.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ELECTROBANK.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Power Banks are portable <link=\"POWER\">Power</link> storage containers that can be used to supply electricity to mobile entities and isolated areas.\n\nSingle-use power banks are easier to produce, but rechargeable and self-charging models are more efficient in the long run.\n\nCautious handling is required, as liquid exposure (or expiration, for self-charging power banks) can lead to explosions."
msgstr "行動電源是可攜式的<link=\"POWER\">電力</link>儲存容器，可以為移動實體和隔離區域供電。\n\n一次性電力儲存器較易生產，但可充電和自充電型號從長遠來看效率更高。\n\n操作時須謹慎，因為暴露在液體中（或自充電電力儲存器的失效）可能導致爆炸。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ELECTROBANK.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ELECTROBANK.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Portable Storage"
msgstr "行動式儲存"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ELECTROBANK.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ELECTROBANK.TITLE"
msgid "Power Banks"
msgstr "行動電源"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EVACUATION.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EVACUATION.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Attention all Gravitas personnel\n\nEvacuation protocol in effect\n\nReactor meltdown in bioengineering imminent\n\nRemain calm and proceed to emergency exits\n\nDo not attempt to use elevators</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>所有引力科技人員注意\n\n啟動疏散程序\n\n生物工程部的反應爐即將熔毀\n\n保持鎮靜並前往緊急出口\n\n不要嘗試使用電梯</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EVACUATION.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EVACUATION.SUBTITLE"
msgid "ENCRYPTION LEVEL: NONE"
msgstr "加密等級：無"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EVACUATION.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EVACUATION.TITLE"
msgid "! EVACUATION NOTICE !"
msgstr "！撤離通知！"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.HEADER_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.HEADER_1"
msgid "Building Rockets"
msgstr "建造火箭"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.HEADER_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.HEADER_2"
msgid "Space Travel"
msgstr "太空旅行"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.HEADER_3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.HEADER_3"
msgid "Space Transport"
msgstr "太空運輸"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.PARAGRAPH_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.PARAGRAPH_1"
msgid "Building a rocket first requires constructing a <link=\"LAUNCHPAD\">Rocket Platform</link> and adding modules from the menu. All rockets will require an engine, a nosecone and a Command Module piloted by a Duplicant possessing the <link=\"ROCKETPILOTING1\">Rocket Piloting</link> skill or higher. Note that the <link=\"HABITATMODULESMALL\">Solo Spacefarer Nosecone</link> functions as both a Command Module and a nosecone.\n\n"
msgstr "建造火箭首先需要建造一個<link=\"LAUNCHPAD\">火箭平台</link>，並從選單中新增模組。所有的火箭都需要引擎、鼻錐和由擁有<link=\"ROCKETPILOTING1\">火箭駕駛</link>技能或更高階技能的複製人駕駛的指揮艙。請注意，<link=\"HABITATMODULESMALL\">單座鼻錐</link>同時具備指揮艙和鼻錐的功能。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.PARAGRAPH_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.PARAGRAPH_2"
msgid "To scan space and see nearby intersteller destinations a <link=\"CLUSTERTELESCOPE\">Telescope</link> must first be built on the surface of a Planetoid. <link=\"ORBITALRESEARCHCENTER\">Orbital Data Collection Lab</link> in orbit around a Planetoid, and <link=\"SCANNERMODULE\">Cartographic Module</link> attached to a rocket can also reveal places on a Starmap.\n\nAlways check engine fuel to determine if your rocket can reach its destination, keeping in mind rockets can only land on Planetoids with a <link=\"LAUNCHPAD\">Rocket Platform</link> on it although some modules like <link=\"SCOUTMODULE\">Rover's Modules</link> and <link=\"PIONEERMODULE\">Trailblazer Modules</link> can be sent to the surface of a Planetoid from a rocket in orbit.\n\n"
msgstr "若要掃描太空並查看附近的星際目的地，首先必須在小行星表面建造一座<link=\"CLUSTERTELESCOPE\">望遠鏡</link>。位於小行星軌道上的<link=\"ORBITALRESEARCHCENTER\">軌道資料收集儀</link>，以及附加於火箭上的<link=\"SCANNERMODULE\">製圖模組</link>，也能揭示星圖上的區域。\n\n務必檢查引擎燃料，以確定你的火箭是否能抵達目的地。請牢記，火箭只能在設有<link=\"LAUNCHPAD\">火箭平台</link>的小行星上著陸；然而，某些模組如<link=\"SCOUTMODULE\">漫遊者模組</link>和<link=\"PIONEERMODULE\">開拓者模組</link>，則可從軌道上的火箭發射至小行星表面。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.PARAGRAPH_3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.PARAGRAPH_3"
msgid "Goods can be teleported between worlds with connected Supply Teleporters through <link=\"ELEMENTSGAS\">Gas</link>, <link=\"ELEMENTSLIQUID\">Liquid</link>, and <link=\"ELEMENTSSOLID\">Solid</link> conduits.\n\nPlanetoids not connected through Supply Teleporters can use rockets to transport goods, either by landing on a <link=\"LAUNCHPAD\">Rocket Platform</link> or a <link=\"ORBITALCARGOMODULE\">Orbital Cargo Module</link> deployed from a rocket in orbit.\n\nAdditionally, the <link=\"RAILGUN\">Interplanetary Launcher</link> can send <link=\"RAILGUNPAYLOAD\">Interplanetary Payloads</link> full of goods through space but must be opened by a <link=\"RAILGUNPAYLOADOPENER\">Payload Opener</link>. A <link=\"LANDINGBEACON\">Targeting Beacon</link> can guide payloads and orbital modules to land at a specific location on a Planetoid surface."
msgstr "貨物可以透過連接補給傳送器上的<link=\"ELEMENTSGAS\">氣體</link>、<link=\"ELEMENTSLIQUID\">液體</link>與<link=\"ELEMENTSSOLID\">固體</link>管道在兩個世界中傳送。\n\n未與補給傳送器連接的小行星，可利用火箭運輸貨物，可以選擇降落在<link=\"LAUNCHPAD\">火箭平台</link>上，或從軌道上的火箭部署<link=\"ORBITALCARGOMODULE\">軌道貨艙模組</link>。此外，<link=\"RAILGUN\">軌道炮</link>能將裝滿貨物的<link=\"RAILGUNPAYLOAD\">星際貨箱</link>送入太空，但需由<link=\"RAILGUNPAYLOADOPENER\">星際貨箱拆箱機</link>打開。<link=\"LANDINGBEACON\">定位信標</link>則可引導貨運艙和軌道模組，降落在小行星表面的特定位置。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASES.TITLE"
msgid "<link=\"EXOBASES\">Space Travel</link>"
msgstr "<link=\"EXOBASES\">太空旅行</link>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASESDLC1.HEADER_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASESDLC1.HEADER_1"
msgid "Building Rockets"
msgstr "建造火箭"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASESDLC1.HEADER_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.EXOBASESDLC1.HEADER_2"
msgid "Space Exploration"
msgstr "太空探索"

