msgid "Moos"
msgstr "飛牛類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GASSYMOO.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GASSYMOO.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Domesticable Critter"
msgstr "可馴養的小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GASSYMOO.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GASSYMOO.TITLE"
msgid "Gassy Moo"
msgstr "瓦斯牛"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.HEADER_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.HEADER_1"
msgid "Plant Mutations"
msgstr "植物變異"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.HEADER_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.HEADER_2"
msgid "Cultivating Mutated Seeds"
msgstr "培育變異種子"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.HEADER_3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.HEADER_3"
msgid "Critter Morphs"
msgstr "小動物變異種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.PARAGRAPH_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.PARAGRAPH_1"
msgid "Plants exposed to radiation sometimes drop mutated seeds when they are harvested. Each type of mutation has its own efficiencies and trade-offs.\n\nMutated seeds can be planted once they have been analyzed in the <link=\"GENETICANALYSISSTATION\">Botanical Analyzer</link>, but the resulting plants will produce no seeds of their own unless they are uprooted.\n\n"
msgstr "暴露於輻射的植物有時會在收成時掉落變異的種子。每種類型的變異都有其自身的效益和好壞。\n\n一旦在<link=\"GENETICANALYSISSTATION\">植物分析儀</link>中分析了變異的種子，就可以種植它們，但產生的植物不會產生自己的種子，除非它們被連根拔起。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.PARAGRAPH_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.PARAGRAPH_2"
msgid "Once mutated seeds have been analyzed in the <link=\"GENETICANALYSISSTATION\">Botanical Analyzer</link>, they are ready to be planted. Continued exposure to naturally occurring radiation or a <link=\"RADIATIONLIGHT\">Radiation Lamp</link> is necessary to prevent wilting.\n\n"
msgstr "突變種子在<link=\"GENETICANALYSISSTATION\">植物分析儀</link>中分析完畢後，即可種植。必須持續暴露於自然發生的輻射或<link=\"RADIATIONLIGHT\">輻射燈</link>下，才能防止枯萎。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.PARAGRAPH_3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.PARAGRAPH_3"
msgid "Variations within a <link=\"CREATURES\">critter</link> species is common, and while they may share some similarities, different members of a species produce different resources and have their own distinct preferences regarding habitats, environmental <link=\"HEAT\">Temperature</link>, and diet.\n\nSee the <link=\"CREATURES::GUIDE\">Field Guide</link> to learn more about caring for critters."
msgstr "<link=\"CREATURES\">生物</link>物種之間的變種是很常見的。雖然牠們可能共享某些相似之處，但同一物種內不同的成員會產生不同的資源，並且對於棲息地、環境<link=\"HEAT\">溫度</link>和飲食有各自獨特的偏好。\n\n請參閱<link=\"CREATURES::GUIDE\">野外指南</link>以了解更多關於照護生物的資訊。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GENETICS.TITLE"
msgid "<link=\"GENETICS\">Genetics</link>"
msgstr "<link=\"GENETICS\">遺傳學</link>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GINGER.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GINGER.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Tonic Root is a close relative of the zingiberaceae family commonly known as ginger. Its heavily burled shoots are typically light brown in colour, and enveloped in a thin layer of protective, edible bark."
msgstr "辛香根是薑科的一員，俗稱生薑。其粗壯的枝條通常呈淺棕色，並包裹在一層薄薄的保護性可食用表皮中。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GINGER.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GINGER.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "In addition to its use as an aromatic culinary ingredient, it has traditionally been employed as a tonic for a variety of minor digestive ailments."
msgstr "除了作為辛香料外，傳統上還被用作各種輕微消化系統疾病的補品。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GINGER.BODY.CONTAINER3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GINGER.BODY.CONTAINER3"
msgid "Its stringy fibers can become irretrievably embedded between one's teeth during mastication."
msgstr "在咀嚼過程中，它的絲狀纖維會深深地卡在牙縫之中。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GINGER.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GINGER.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GINGER.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GINGER.TITLE"
msgid "Tonic Root"
msgstr "辛香根"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GLOSSY.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GLOSSY.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Pictured: \"Glossy\" Drecko variant</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>圖為：「滑鱗」蜥變種</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GLOSSY.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GLOSSY.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Morph"
msgstr "小動物變種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GLOSSY.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GLOSSY.TITLE"
msgid "Glossy Drecko"
msgstr "滑鱗蜥"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GRUBFRUITPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GRUBFRUITPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Grubfruit Plant exhibits a coevolutionary relationship with the <link=\"DIVERGENTSPECIES\">Divergent</link> species.\n\nThough capable of producing fruit without the help of the Divergent, the <link=\"WORMPLANT\">Spindly Grubfruit</link> is a substandard version of the Grubfruit in both taste and caloric value per cycle.\n\nThe mechanism for how the Divergent inspires Grubfruit Plant growth is not entirely known but is thought to be somehow tied to the infrasonic 'songs' these insects lovingly purr to their plants."
msgstr "蟲蜜草與<link=\"DIVERGENTSPECIES\">變異蟲</link>物種之間形成共同演化的關係。\n\n雖然能夠在沒有變異蟲幫助下也能生產果實，但<link=\"WORMPLANT\">劣質蟲蜜果</link>在美味與熱量方面都輸給正常的蟲蜜果。\n\n變異蟲們如何刺激蟲蜜草成長的機制尚未完全清楚，但被認為以某種方式親切向植物發出一種次聲波的「歌聲」。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GRUBFRUITPLANT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GRUBFRUITPLANT.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GRUBFRUITPLANT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GRUBFRUITPLANT.TITLE"
msgid "Grubfruit Plant"
msgstr "蟲蜜草"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GUMWOOD.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GUMWOOD.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Gum Wood is a flexible type of <link=\"WOODLOG\">Wood</link> with the unique sap that can be used in the production of <link=\"RUBBER\">Rubber</link>.\n\nNote that it is not <i>made</i> of rubber, and thus will not bounce when thrown."
msgstr "黏膠木材是一種柔韌的<link=\"WOODLOG\">木材</link>，其獨特的樹脂可用於生產<link=\"RUBBER\">橡膠</link>。\n\n請注意，它並非<i>由</i>橡膠構成，因此扔出去時並不會彈跳。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GUMWOOD.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GUMWOOD.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Renewable Resource"
msgstr "可再生資源"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.GUMWOOD.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.GUMWOOD.TITLE"
msgid "Gum Wood"
msgstr "粘膠木材"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.HARDSKINBERRYPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.HARDSKINBERRYPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Pikeapple Bush produces a nutritious fruit distantly related to those in the Durio genus.\n\nThose who find the Pikeapple pulp's fragrance overwhelming should consume their portion whilst standing near the plant itself; the shrubbery's gentle swaying produces a wafting effect that promotes air circulation.\n\nClosed-toe footwear is recommended, as barefoot contact with the plant's sharp seeds inevitably leads to infection."
msgstr "刺殼果灌木能產生一種營養豐富的果實，與榴槤屬的關係較遠。\n\n那些發現刺殼果果肉的撲鼻香氣的人應當站在植株附近將其吃完；灌木輕微搖曳能產生一種吹拂效果，促進空氣流動。\n\n建議穿不露腳趾的鞋，因為赤腳接觸這種植物的尖銳種子會不可避免地導致感染。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.HARDSKINBERRYPLANT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.HARDSKINBERRYPLANT.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.HARDSKINBERRYPLANT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.HARDSKINBERRYPLANT.TITLE"
msgid "Pikeapple Bush"
msgstr "刺殼果灌木"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.HATCH.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.HATCH.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Hatch has no eyes and is completely blind, although a photosensitive patch atop its head is capable of detecting even minor changes in overhead light, making it prefer dark caves and tunnels."
msgstr "哈奇沒有眼睛，是完全失明的。雖說頭上感光部位可以偵測微量的光線變化，但使其更喜歡待在黑暗的洞穴與通道。"

