#. STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC3_POTATOBATTERY.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC3_POTATOBATTERY.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>[Voice Recognition Initialized]\n[Subject Identified: B577]</smallcaps>\n\n[LOG BEGINS]\n\nA recent conversation with our colleagues over in the electrical engineering department has highlighted exciting potential applications for our crops.\n\nThey're seeking alternative inputs for the new universal power bank prototypes...\n\n...a passing remark about the potato batteries of our youth led to talk of biobatteries and bacterial nanowires.\n\n...tuberous plants are promising candidates for electrochemical batteries. Our lab-grown specimens are distinct from the humble solanum tuberosum in appearance and texture, but some may still function as acidic electrolytes.\n\nThere are so many avenues to investigate, and so little time...\n\n[LOG ENDS]\n------------------\n"
msgstr "<smallcaps>[語音辨識系統初始化完成]\n[主體已識別：B577]</smallcaps>\n\n[日誌開始]\n\n最近與我們電氣工程部的同事進行了一次對話，強調了我們的作物令人興奮的潛在應用。\n\n他們正在為新的通用行動電源原型體尋找替代材料……\n\n……幾個年輕人關於馬鈴薯電池的隨口一談，引發了大家對生物電池和細菌奈米導線的討論\n\n……塊莖植物是電化學電池最有可能的候選。我們實驗室培育的樣本在外觀和質地上與普通的馬鈴薯不同，但其中一些仍可能起到酸性電解質的作用。\n\n有太多調查的途徑，但時間又少得可憐……\n\n[日誌結束]\n------------------\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC3_POTATOBATTERY.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC3_POTATOBATTERY.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "<smallcaps>[Log fragmentation detected]\n[Voice Recognition unavailable]</smallcaps>\n\n[LOG BEGINS]\n\n...is it unethical to ask a hungry colony to choose between using edible crops for sustenance or for power production? Of course not.\n\nOur task is to provide as many options for survival as possible, not to dictate which options are morally superior.\n\nThe real question is whether or not the AI guide will be sufficiently advanced to notify them that the choices exist...\n\n...and whether single-use bio power banks that vaporize due to extreme thermal runaway will truly be the difference between a successful colony and an...<i>unsuccessful</i>...one.\n\n[LOG ENDS]\n------------------\n"
msgstr "<smallcaps>[偵測到日誌片段]\n[語音辨識系統無法使用]</smallcaps>\n\n[日誌開始]\n\n……要求飢餓的殖民地，將可食用作物用於維持生計和電力生產之間做出選擇，是否有悖人倫？當然不是。\n\n我們的任務是提供儘可能多的生存選擇，而不是規定哪些選擇在道德上更優越。\n\n真正的問題是人工智慧的指導是否足夠先進，能夠告知他們選擇是存在的……\n\n……以及由於極端熱失控而蒸發的一次性生物行動電源，是否真的會在成功的殖民地和……<b>沒成功的</b>……殖民地之間有實際區別。\n\n[日誌結束]\n------------------\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC3_POTATOBATTERY.BODY.CONTAINER3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC3_POTATOBATTERY.BODY.CONTAINER3"
msgid "<smallcaps>[Log fragmentation detected]\n[Voice Recognition unavailable]</smallcaps>\n\n[LOG BEGINS]\n\n...word of our efforts has spread!\n\nThe bioengineers report that some of their creatures' eggs contain phosphorescent albumen that requires only basic processing in order to trigger chemical reactions that produce storable energy. It displays unprecedented biocompatibility with the prosthetics Dr. Gossmann has been developing.\n\nThe Director assigned us a half-dozen new graduates last week. They work the night shift—this generation never sleeps!\n\nNo one has met them yet, but their data is always neatly compiled for us to find in the morning.\n\nThey seem determined to prioritize the use of metallic and radioactive components rather than plant or animal-based ones.\n\nYouthful idealism, perhaps?\n\nNevertheless, their findings <i>are</i> quite compelling.\n\nI admire their mettle.\n\n[LOG ENDS]\n------------------\n"
msgstr "<smallcaps>[偵測到日誌片段]\n[語音辨識系統無法使用]</smallcaps>\n\n[日誌開始]\n\n……我們成果的訊息已經傳開了！\n\n生物工程師報告說，他們的一些生物的卵含有磷光蛋白，只需進行基本處理即可引發產生可儲存能量的化學反應。它與 Gossmann 博士正在開發的義肢表現出前所未有的生物相容性。\n\n上週，總監給我們分配了六名應屆畢業生。他們負責夜班——這些年輕人從不睡覺！\n\n還沒有人見過他們，但他們的數據總是整齊地整理好，以便我們早上找到。\n\n他們似乎更傾向於使用金屬和放射性成分，而不是植物或動物成分。\n\n也許是年輕人的理想主義吧？\n\n不過，他們的發現<b>確實</b>很有說服力。\n\n我欽佩他們的勇氣。\n\n[日誌結束]\n------------------\n"

