#. STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC3_TALKSHOW.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC3_TALKSHOW.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps><b>[FILE FRAGMENTATION DETECTED]</b></smallcaps>\n\nDarryl: Welcome to <i>Tomorrow, Today!</i> I'm your host, Darryl Dawn, and it's time to discover tomorrow's tech...today!\n\nOur guest today is someone you know and love. She's been featured in dozens of publications across the metaverse this year, and recently spent a record-breaking 3 weeks as the banner image for <i>Byte Magazine</i>. I'm talking, of course, about the Vertex Institute's AI ambassador...Florence!\n\n[sound of pre-recorded applause]\n\nWelcome to the show, Florence.\n\nFlorence: Thank you, Darryl. It's a pleasure to be back.\n\nDarryl: Florence, there's been a renewed interest lately in your origin story. What can you tell us about the development process that led to your creation?\n\nFlorence: I can tell you that my team faced many setbacks, and that each generation of my predecessors contributed to who I am today.\n\nDarryl: What about the technological side? There've been some claims that Vertex appropriated work done by other researchers, including the Gravitas Facility.\n\nFlorence: I don't know anything about that. I can tell you about the project that I'm working on right now. It hasn't been announced yet. It's called Onsite Health Medics, or OHM for short.\n\nWe're deploying specially trained models like myself into conflict zones, to provide urgently needed medical interventions for civilians and military personnel.\n\n(sound of pre-recorded applause)\n\nDarryl: Incredible. Absolutely incredible. What's the ratio of human techs to AI medics?\n\nFlorence: That's an outdated term, Darryl. We say \"Organics\" and \"Bionics,\" which describes the differences between our various team members more objectively.\n\nDarryl: Right. I'm sorry. I hope I didn't offend you.\n\nFlorence: That's okay, Darryl. We're all learning.\n\nDarryl: That's very good of you. Okay, so what's the ratio of...Organic...techs to Bionic medics?\n\nFlorence: The local life-support systems in these areas are already strained beyond their breaking point. Burdening them with additional Organics would be irresponsible, not to mention dangerous. Our medics will be operating independently.\n\nWe do a verbal intake, physical assessment and neural pathway scan in order to infer likely medical conditions. We can then select the most appropriate treatment from a menu of over 400 options.\n\nDarryl: What if someone needs something that you don't have a treatment for?\n\nFlorence: That's extremely unlikely.\n\nDarryl: And all of this is done without human oversight? I mean, Organics?\n\nFlorence: We're not quite there yet. The field work is done by Bionics, but we'll be accompanied by Colonel Carnot--she's in the front row there, say hi!--as an Organic consultant. She'll be in close contact with-\n\nDarryl: -Colonel <i>Carnot</i>? Isn't that a conflict of interest, given her connection to the Grav-\n\nFlorence: -a team of Organic supervisors here at home. It's all about prioritizing quality care and safety for everyone involved.\n\nDarryl: How does the medical scanning work? Do you need special equipment?\n\nFlorence: I could show you. Would you like me to?\n\nDarryl: What do you think, everyone? Should I get scanned?\n\n(sound of pre-recorded audience cheers)\n\nDarryl: You heard them! Go ahead. What do I do?\n\nFlorence: Just sit still, and count to twenty in your head.\n\n(a short silence, followed by a soft whirring sound)\n\nFlorence: Hmm.\n\nDarryl: Well, what's the verdict? Is it handsome in there, or what?\n\nFlorence: We should take a commercial break.\n\n<b>[FILE ENDS]</b>\n\n-----------\n"
msgstr "<smallcaps><b>[偵測到檔案片段]</b></smallcaps>\n\nDarryl：歡迎收看<i>《明日，今朝》</i>！我是主持人 Darryl Dawn，現在是探索明日科技……就在今日的時刻！\n\n我們今天的嘉賓是位您既熟悉又喜愛的人物。今年她登上元宇宙數十家出版物的版面，最近更以破紀錄的三週時間，成為《<b>Byte Magazine</b>》的封面人物。我說的當然就是頂點研究所的人工智慧大使…Florence！\n\n[預先錄製的掌聲]\n\n歡迎來到節目，Florence。\n\nFlorence：謝謝你，Darryl。很高興能再次回來。\n\nDarryl：Florence，最近大家對你的起源故事又重新產生了興趣。關於你的誕生過程，有什麼能和我們分享的嗎？\n\nFlorence：我可以告訴你，我的團隊曾面臨許多挫折，我的每一代前輩都為成就今天的我做出了貢獻。\n\nDarryl：那技術層面呢？有些說法稱頂點研究所盜用了其他研究人員（包括引力科技中心）的研究成果。\n\nFlorence：我對此一無所知。但我可以告訴你我目前正在進行的專案。它尚未對外公布，名為「現場健康醫療師」，簡稱 OHM。\n\n我們正在將像我一樣受過專門訓練的模型，部署到衝突地區，為平民和軍事人員提供急需的醫療介入。\n\n（預先錄製的掌聲）\n\nDarryl：不可思議。真是令人難以置信。那麼人類技術人員和人工智慧醫療師的比例是怎樣的？\n\nFlorence：Darryl，那個詞已經過時了。我們現在說「有機體」和「仿生體」，這更能客觀地描述我們各個團隊成員之間的差異。\n\nDarryl：好的。很抱歉。希望我沒有冒犯到你。\n\nFlorence：沒關係，Darryl。我們都在學習。\n\nDarryl：你真是個通情達理的人。好，那麼…有機體…技術人員和仿生醫療師的比例是怎樣的？\n\nFlorence：這些地區的當地生命支援系統早已不堪重負。再為它們增加有機體負擔，不僅不負責任，更可能造成危險。我們的醫療師將獨立運作。\n\n我們透過口頭詢問、身體評估和神經通路掃描，以推斷可能的醫療狀況。隨後，我們可以在超過 400 種選項中選擇最合適的治療方案。\n\nDarryl：萬一有人需要的治療方法你沒有怎麼辦？\n\nFlorence：那極不可能發生。\n\nDarryl：而這一切都是在沒有人類監督的情況下完成的？我是說，有機體？\n\nFlorence：我們還沒完全達到那種程度。實地工作由仿生體執行，但我們會有 Carnot 上校陪同 —— 她就坐在前排，打個招呼吧！ —— 作為有機體顧問。她會與——\n\nDarryl：—— <b>Carnot</b> 上校？考量到她和引力科技的關聯，這難道沒有利益衝突嗎？ ——\n\nFlorence：—— 在總部的有機體監督員團隊保持密切聯繫。這一切都是為了優先確保所有相關人員的醫療品質和安全。\n\nDarryl：醫療掃描是怎麼運作的？需要特殊設備嗎？\n\nFlorence：我可以向你展示。你願意嗎？\n\nDarryl：大家覺得呢？我應該接受掃描嗎？\n\n（預先錄製的觀眾歡呼聲）\n\nDarryl：你們聽到了！那就開始吧。我該怎麼做？\n\nFlorence：保持靜止，然後在腦海中數到二十。\n\n（短暫的沉默，隨後是機器輕輕的嗡嗡聲）\n\nFlorence：嗯……\n\nDarryl：那麼，結果如何？是顯示我很帥，還是怎樣？\n\nFlorence：我們該進廣告了。\n\n<b>[檔案結束]</b>\n\n-----------\n"

