#. STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC5_CAKEANDTEA.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.INVESTIGATIONS.DLC5_CAKEANDTEA.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Ellie: Happy birthday, nerd!\n\nJosh: Is this... the exact same cake I got you for your birthday?\n\nEllie: So what? It was a good cake. Do you want some or not?\n\nJosh: I mean, yeah! It's just funny that you got me your favorite cake for my birthday.\n\nEllie: If I'm paying for it, I may as well enjoy it.\n\nJosh: You can see why it's weird though, right?\n\nEllie: Fine, whatever. You wanna pile on with everyone else and say I'm the worst, go ahead.\n\nJosh: I didn't say that!\n\nEllie: I may not be, like, <i>imprisoned</i> by social niceties, but I have a pretty good grasp of basic human decency. Which is more than I can say for <i>some</i> people.\n\nJosh: Ellie, I'm really not- wait, like who?\n\nEllie: Ha! I knew it. You're just as gossipy as me!\n\nJosh: I'll give you the first slice if you tell me.\n\nEllie: Deal. Okay, you know that hippie ocean scientist Director Stern brought in?\n\nJosh: The guy who was teaching us box breathing in the cafeteria?\n\nEllie: Probably. He's somewhere at the bottom of the Pacific right now. Anyway, you CANNOT tell anyone, but-\n\nJosh: He's what??\n\nEllie: He's not <i>dead</i>, dummy. He's on the Paladin with Frankie all summer. They're de-extincting amoeba or plankton or whatever.\n\nJosh: Whew. Okay. What'd he do? I thought he seemed nice.\n\nEllie: If you stopped interrupting every two seconds, maybe you'd find out.\n\nJosh: Sorryyyyyyy.\n\nEllie: I caught him recording a meeting with the Director. He came out of her office and checked a weird little device in his chest pocket. He looked <i>very</i> awkward when he realized I was standing right there.\n\nEllie: He asked me where Dr. Broussard's office was, and he got really mad that she didn't work here? Like, chill! Why did you assume she did?\n\nJosh: Who's Dr. Broussard?\n\nEllie: Seriously? Six-time winner of the Science for Humanity Prize? You really do live under a rock.\n\nJosh:  Okay, okay. So...is that it? He was just... <i>maybe</i> recording... and disappointed that someone doesn't work here?\n\nEllie: He didn't even say THANK YOU, Josh.\n\nJosh: Right. What a monster.\n\nEllie: Exactly."
msgstr "Ellie：生日快樂，書呆子！\n\nJosh：這……這是不是跟我送你的那個一模一樣的蛋糕？\n\nEllie：那又怎樣？那蛋糕很好吃。你到底要不要吃？\n\nJosh：我是要吃！只是覺得挺好笑的，你居然買你自己最愛吃的蛋糕來給我過生日。\n\nEllie：既然是我掏錢買的，我總得享受一下吧。\n\nJosh：不過你能理解這有點怪吧？\n\nEllie：行行行，隨便啦。你要跟其他人一樣數落我，說我是個爛人，那就請便吧。\n\nJosh：我可沒那麼說！\n\nEllie：我可能確實不怎麼被社交禮儀束縛，但我對為人最基本的體面還是有數的。這可比某些人強多了。\n\nJosh：Ellie，我真的不是——等等，你是指誰？\n\nEllie：哈！我就知道。你跟我一樣八卦！\n\nJosh：你要是肯告訴我，第一塊蛋糕給你。\n\nEllie：成交。好吧，你知道 Stern 總監請來的那個嬉皮士海洋科學家嗎？\n\nJosh：就是在食堂教我們箱式呼吸法的那個傢伙？\n\nEllie：應該就是他。他現在人在太平洋海底某處。反正，你絕對不能告訴別人，不過——\n\nJosh：他怎麼了？？\n\nEllie：他又不是死了，傻瓜。他一整個夏天都跟 Frankie 待在聖騎士號上。他們在搞什麼復活阿米巴原蟲還是什麼浮游生物之類的。\n\nJosh：呼，好吧。他到底幹了什麼？我覺得他看起來人挺好的啊。\n\nEllie：你要是能別每隔兩秒打斷我一次，說不定就知道了。\n\nJosh：對不起嘛。\n\nEllie：我撞見他在錄跟主管開會的錄音。他從主管辦公室出來，檢查了一個藏在胸前口袋裡的奇怪小裝置。發現我就站在旁邊的時候，他表情特別尷尬。\n\nEllie：他問我 Broussard 博士的辦公室在哪兒，然後聽說她不在這兒工作就特別生氣？拜託！他為什麼認定她在這兒工作啊？\n\nJosh：Dr. Broussard 是誰？\n\nEllie：不是吧？人文科學獎的六屆得主？你還真是與世隔絕。\n\nJosh：好吧好吧。所以……就這樣？他就是……可能錄了音……然後因為有人不在這兒工作而失望？\n\nEllie：他連句謝謝都沒說，Josh。\n\nJosh：是啊。真是個惡魔。\n\nEllie：正是。"

