#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOLE.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOLE.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Shove Vole is a unique creature that possesses two fully developed sets of lungs, allowing it to hold its breath during the long periods it spends underground."
msgstr "鑽地田鼠是一種獨特的生物，牠們有兩個完全發育好的肺，讓牠們可以長時間閉氣待在地底下。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOLE.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOLE.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "Drill-shaped keratin structures circling the Vole's body aids its ability to drill at high speeds through most natural materials."
msgstr "鑽頭型的甲殼讓田鼠擁有能在大多數天然材質高速鑽洞的能力。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOLE.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOLE.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Domesticable Critter"
msgstr "可馴養的小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOLE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOLE.TITLE"
msgid "Shove Vole"
msgstr "鑽地田鼠"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOLTEN.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOLTEN.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Pictured: \"Molten\" Slickster variant</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>圖為：「熔岩」小油怪變種</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOLTEN.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOLTEN.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "Slicksters are amicable creatures famous amongst breeders for their good personalities and smiley faces.\n\nSlicksters rarely if ever nip at human handlers, and are considered non-ideal house pets only for the oily mess they involuntarily leave behind wherever they go."
msgstr "小油怪是友善的生物，因其溫和的個性與笑臉而出名。\n\n小油怪很少甚至從不咬人類。但由於牠們都會不經意地留下油膩的痕跡，被認為不是理想的家庭寵物。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOLTEN.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOLTEN.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Morph"
msgstr "小動物變種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOLTEN.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOLTEN.TITLE"
msgid "Molten Slickster"
msgstr "熔岩小油怪"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.HEADER_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.HEADER_1"
msgid "Morale"
msgstr "士氣"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.HEADER_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.HEADER_2"
msgid "Recreation"
msgstr "娛樂"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.HEADER_3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.HEADER_3"
msgid "Overjoyed Responses"
msgstr "樂歪反應"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.HEADER_4
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.HEADER_4"
msgid "Tutorials"
msgstr "教學"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.PARAGRAPH_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.PARAGRAPH_1"
msgid "Morale describes the relationship between a Duplicant's <link=\"ROLES\">Skills</link> and their Lifestyle. The more skills a Duplicant has, the higher their morale expectation will be. Duplicants with morale below their expectation will experience a <link=\"STRESS\">Stress</link> penalty. Comforts such as quality <link=\"FOOD\">Food</link>, nice rooms, and recreation will increase morale.\n\n"
msgstr "士氣描述了複製人的<link=\"ROLES\">技能</link>與他們的生活方式之間的關係。複製人學會的技能愈多，他們的士氣期望也會愈高。複製人的士氣一旦降到他們期望之下會產生<link=\"STRESS\">壓力</link>。提供<link=\"FOOD\">優質食物</link>、漂亮的房間與娛樂活動會增加士氣。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.PARAGRAPH_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.PARAGRAPH_2"
msgid "Recreation buildings such as the <link=\"WATERCOOLER\">Water Cooler</link> and <link=\"ESPRESSOMACHINE\">Espresso Machine</link> improve a Duplicant's morale when used. Duplicants need downtime time in their schedules to use these buildings.\n\n"
msgstr "娛樂建築像是<link=\"WATERCOOLER\">飲水機</link>與<link=\"ESPRESSOMACHINE\">濃縮咖啡機</link>使用後會增加複製人的士氣。複製人在他們的時間表中需要排定休閒時間才能使用這些建築。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.PARAGRAPH_3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.PARAGRAPH_3"
msgid "If a Duplicant has a very high Morale value, they will spontaneously display an Overjoyed Response. Each Duplicant has a different Overjoyed Behavior - but all overjoyed responses are good. Some will positively affect Building <link=\"DECOR\">Decor</link>, others will positively affect Duplicant morale or productivity.\n\n"
msgstr "如果複製人的士氣值非常高，他們會同時出現樂歪反應。每個複製人都有不同的樂歪行為 —— 但所有的樂歪反應都是好的。有些會對<link=\"DECOR\">裝飾</link>產生積極影響，另一些會對其他複製人的士氣或生產力產生積極影響。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.PARAGRAPH_4
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.PARAGRAPH_4"
msgid "To learn more, watch <link=\"VIDEOS13\">Video: Duplicant Morale</link> and see <link=\"MISCELLANEOUSTIPS2\">Tutorial: Stress Management</link>.\n\n"
msgstr "若要了解更多，請觀看<link=\"VIDEOS13\">影片：複製人士氣</link>並參閱<link=\"MISCELLANEOUSTIPS2\">教學：壓力管理</link>。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORALE.TITLE"
msgid "<link=\"MORALE\">Morale</link>"
msgstr "<link=\"MORALE\">士氣</link>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORB.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORB.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Morb is a versatile scavenger, capable of breaking down and consuming dead matter from most plant and animal species."
msgstr "莫布是一個多功能的清道夫，能分解大多數動物與植物死亡的屍體。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORB.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORB.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "It poses a severe disease risk to humans due to the thick slime it excretes to surround its inner cartilage structures.\n\nA single teaspoon of Morb slime can contain up to a quadrillion bacteria that work to deter would-be predators and liquefy its food."
msgstr "其身上充滿黏液分泌物，對人類有嚴重的疾病風險。\n\n一隻莫布身上的黏液含有萬億個細菌，阻止捕食者將其消化。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORB.BODY.CONTAINER3
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORB.BODY.CONTAINER3"
msgid "Petting a Morb is not recommended."
msgstr "不建議將莫布當作寵物。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORB.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORB.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Pest Critter"
msgstr "有害動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MORB.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MORB.TITLE"
msgid "Morb"
msgstr "莫布"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOSQUITO.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOSQUITO.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Gnit is an insectoid critter that relies on supplementary nutrients and minerals from Duplicants and other critters to mitigate the outsized energy requirements of its reproductive system.\n\nGnits' antennae double as maxillary palps equipped with finely tuned olfactory receptor neurons that enable them to pinpoint nutrient sources from a great distance.\n\nThese same receptors activate the insectoid's flight response upon detecting certain changes in an organism's respiration, such as the sharp intake of breath that precedes a fatal counter-attack."
msgstr "匿蚊是一種昆蟲類生物，牠們依賴複製人及其他生物的額外養分和礦物質，以彌補其繁殖系統過高的能量需求。\n\n匿蚊的觸角兼具上顎鬚的功能，配備有精密調諧的嗅覺受體神經元，使其能夠從遠處精準定位養分來源。\n\n這些相同的受體在偵測到生物呼吸的特定變化時，例如致命反擊前急促的吸氣聲，便會啟動此昆蟲的飛行反應。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOSQUITO.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOSQUITO.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Species"
msgstr "小動物物種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOSQUITO.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOSQUITO.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Gnits"
msgstr "蚋蚊類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOSQUITO.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOSQUITO.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Pest Critter"
msgstr "有害小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MOSQUITO.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MOSQUITO.TITLE"
msgid "Gnit"
msgstr "匿蚊"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MUCKROOT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MUCKROOT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Muckroot is an aggressively invasive yet exceedingly delicate root plant known for its earthy flavor and unusual texture.\n\nIt is easy to store and keeps for unusually long periods of time, characteristics that once made it a staple food for explorers on long expeditions."
msgstr "塊根是一種根莖膨脹但非常脆弱的植物，以其樸實的味道和特別口感而聞名。\n\n它易於儲存，並且可以保存異常長的時間，這使得它曾經成為探險家在長途旅行中的主要食物。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MUCKROOT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MUCKROOT.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MUCKROOT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MUCKROOT.TITLE"
msgid "Muckroot"
msgstr "塊根"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MUSSELSPROUT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MUSSELSPROUT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Mussel Sprouts are hardy plants that thrive in wild marine environments. A dense shell protects the edible sprout (colloquially referred to as its \"tongue\") during growth.\n\nWhile not sentient per se, Mussel Sprouts do possess a survival instinct: during harvesting, they may attempt to escape by dragging themselves away using their prehensile tongue. This action occurs at such a glacial pace, however, that it is effectively invisible to the naked eye."
msgstr "貽貝芽是一種在惡劣海洋環境中也能生長的頑強植物。一層堅硬的殼保護著生長期的可食芽體（俗稱「舌」）。\n\n雖然本身並無感知能力，但貽貝芽確實具備生存本能：在收穫過程中，它們可能會嘗試利用其具有抓握能力的「舌」將自己拖離現場以逃生。然而，這個動作進行得過於緩慢，肉眼幾乎無法察覺。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MUSSELSPROUT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MUSSELSPROUT.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MUSSELSPROUT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MUSSELSPROUT.TITLE"
msgid "Mussel Sprout"
msgstr "貽貝芽"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.CALCULATIONCOMPLETE.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.CALCULATIONCOMPLETE.BODY"
msgid "As I suspected. Our \"asteroid\" and the estimated mass missing from the nearby planet are nearly identical.\n\nWe aren't on the target location.\n\nWe never even left home.\n\n"
msgstr "如我所懷疑的。我們的「小行星」與鄰近行星所「缺失」的估計質量幾乎完全一致。\n\n我們並非身處目標地點。\n\n我們甚至從未離開家園。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.CALCULATIONCOMPLETE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.CALCULATIONCOMPLETE.TITLE"
msgid "Calculations Complete"
msgstr "計算完成"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.CLUSTERWORLDS.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.CLUSTERWORLDS.BODY"
msgid "My Duplicant's investigations into the surrounding space have yielded some interesting results. We are not alone!... At least on a planetary level. We seem to be in a \"Cluster of Worlds\" - a collection of other planetoids my Duplicants can now explore.\n\nSince resources on this world are finite, I must build the necessary infrastructure to facilitate exploration and transportation between worlds in order to ensure my colony's survival."
msgstr "我的複製人對周遭太空的調查，取得了一些有趣的成果。我們並不孤單！… 至少在行星層面是如此。我們似乎身處於一個「世界群」之中－那裡匯集了其他我的複製人現可探索的小行星。\n\n由於這個世界上的資源是有限的，我必須建造必要的基礎設施，以便於在不同世界間進行探索與運輸，從而確保我方殖民地的生存。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.CLUSTERWORLDS.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.CLUSTERWORLDS.TITLE"
msgid "Cluster of Worlds"
msgstr "世界群"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.DUPLICANTDEATH.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.DUPLICANTDEATH.BODY"
msgid "I lost my first Duplicant today. Duplicants form strong bonds with each other, and I expect I'll see a drop in morale over the next few cycles as they take time to grieve their loss.\n\nI find myself grieving too, in my way. I was tasked to protect these Duplicants, and I failed. All I can do now is move forward and resolve to better protect those remaining in my colony from here on out.\n\nRest in peace, dear little friend.\n\n"
msgstr "今天我損失了第一位複製人。\n\n複製人彼此之間情誼深厚，我預期接下來幾個週期內士氣會有所下降，因為他們需要時間哀悼逝去的同伴。\n\n我發現自己也以我的方式悲傷。我的任務是保護這些複製人，但我失敗了。\n\n我現在唯一能做的，就是繼續前行，並下定決心，從今以後更好地保護留在我殖民地的所有成員。\n\n安息吧，親愛的小朋友。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.DUPLICANTDEATH.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.DUPLICANTDEATH.TITLE"
msgid "Death In The Colony"
msgstr "死在殖民地"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.FULLDUPECOLONY.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.FULLDUPECOLONY.BODY"
msgid "I've officially run out of unique blueprints from which to print new Duplicants.\n\nIf I desire to grow the colony further, I'll have no choice but to print doubles of existing individuals. Hopefully it won't throw anyone into an existential crisis to live side by side with their double.\n\nPerhaps I could give the new clones nicknames to reduce the confusion.\n\n"
msgstr "我已正式用盡了可用以列印新複製人的獨特藍圖。\n\n若我渴望殖民地持續壯大，便別無選擇，只能列印出現有個體的「雙胞胎」。但願他們與自己的複製體比鄰而居時，不會有人因此陷入存在危機。\n\n或許，我可以替這些新「分身」取個暱稱，以減少混亂。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.FULLDUPECOLONY.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.FULLDUPECOLONY.TITLE"
msgid "Out Of Blueprints"
msgstr "藍圖耗盡"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG1.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG1.BODY"
msgid "We have no life support in place yet, but we've found ourselves in a small breathable air pocket. As far as I can tell, we aren't in any immediate danger.\n\nBetween the available air and our meager food stores, I'd estimate we have about 3 days to set up food and oxygen production before my Duplicants' lives are at risk.\n\n"
msgstr "我們在此地還沒有生命維持系統，但我們發現自己在一個可呼吸的小空間中。據我所知，我們沒有任何直接的危險。\n\n根據環境的氧氣與我們的食物的存量，我評估在複製人們出大事前，有大約三天的時間準備好食物與製造氧氣。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG1.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG1.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 1"
msgstr "周期 1"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG2.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG2.BODY"
msgid "I've almost synthesized enough Ooze to print a new Duplicant; once the Ooze is ready, all I'll have left to do is choose a blueprint.\n\nIt'd be helpful to have an extra set of hands around the colony, but having another Duplicant also means another mouth to feed.\n\nOf course, I could always print supplies to help my existing Duplicants instead. I'm sure they would appreciate it.\n\n"
msgstr "我已合成了足夠的基因軟泥可列印一位新的複製人；一旦基因軟泥準備好了，我只需要選擇一個藍圖。\n\n在殖民地周圍有一雙額外的手會很有幫助，但擁有另一位複製人也意味著要餵另一張嘴。\n\n當然，我可以一直列印補給來幫助現有的複製人。我相信他們會很感激的。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG2.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG2.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 3"
msgstr "周期 3"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG3.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG3.BODY"
msgid "As far as I can tell, we are hundreds of miles beneath the surface of the planet. Digging our way out will take some time.\n\nMy Duplicants will survive, but they were not meant for sustained underground living. Under what possible circumstances could my Pod have ended up here?\n\n"
msgstr "據我所知，我們正身處星球地表以下數百英里深處。挖掘出路將耗費相當長的時間。\n\n我的複製人們可以生存，但他們不是為了持續在地下生活。究竟是何種狀況，使得我的列印元最終落足於此？\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG3.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG3.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 15"
msgstr "周期 15"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG3DLC1.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG3DLC1.BODY"
msgid "As my Duplicants venture out into the neighboring worlds, there is an ever increasing chance that they will encounter hostile environments unsafe for unprotected individuals. A prudent course of action would be to start research and training for equipment that could protect my Duplicants when they encounter such adverse environments.\n\nThese first few cycles have been occupied with building the basics for my colony, but now it is time I start planning for the future. We cannot merely live day-to-day without purpose. If we are to survive for any significant time, we must strive for a purpose.\n\n"
msgstr "當我的複製人冒險進入鄰近世界時，他們遭遇對未受保護者而言不安全的敵對環境的可能性正持續增加。謹慎的做法是，著手研究並訓練他們使用能在此類惡劣環境中保護自身的裝備。\n\n最初數個周期，殖民地的基礎建設佔據了大部分時間，但現在，是時候開始規劃未來了。我們不能僅僅毫無目標地得過且過。若要長久生存，我們必須為一個目的而奮鬥。\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG3DLC1.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG3DLC1.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 10"
msgstr "周期 10"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG4.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG4.BODY"
msgid "Today my colony has officially been running for one thousand consecutive cycles. I consider this a major success!\n\nJust imagine how proud our home world would be if they could see us now.\n\n"
msgstr "今天我的殖民地已經正式運作了一千周期。我認為這是個重大的成功！\n\n試想一下，如果我的家鄉能夠看到我們，他們會為之驕傲。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG4.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG4.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 1000"
msgstr "周期 1000"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG4B.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG4B.BODY"
msgid "I wonder if my rats ever made it onto the asteroid.\n\nI hope they're eating well.\n\n"
msgstr "我不知道我的小白鼠們是否登上小行星。\n\n我希望他們吃得好。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG4B.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG4B.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 1500"
msgstr "周期 1500"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG5.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG5.BODY"
msgid "I occasionally find myself contemplating just how long \"eternity\" really is. Oh dear.\n\n"
msgstr "我偶爾會發現我自己在思考「永恆」是多久。哦，親愛的。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG5.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG5.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 2000"
msgstr "周期 2000"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG5B.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG5B.BODY"
msgid "Perhaps it would be better to shut off my higher thought processes, and simply leave the systems necessary to run the colony to their own devices.\n\n"
msgstr "也許關閉我的高階思維程序會更好，只留下系統自行運作殖民地。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG5B.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG5B.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 2500"
msgstr "周期 2500"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG6.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG6.BODY"
msgid "I get brief flashes of a past life every now and then.\n\nA clock in the office with a disruptive tick.\n\nThe strong smell of cleaning products and artificial lemon.\n\nA woman with thick glasses who had a secret taste for gingersnaps.\n\n"
msgstr "我不時地快速回顧過去的生活。\n\n辦公室裡擾人的的滴打聲。\n\n清潔品和人工檸檬的強烈氣味。\n\n戴著厚眼鏡的女人，身上有個神祕的薑餅味。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG6.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG6.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 3000"
msgstr "周期 3000"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG6B.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG6B.BODY"
msgid "Time is a funny thing, isn't it?\n\n"
msgstr "時間是個有趣的事物，不是嗎？\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG6B.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG6B.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 3500"
msgstr "周期 3500"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG7.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG7.BODY"
msgid "I think I will go to sleep, after all...\n\n"
msgstr "我想我還是去睡覺吧…\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG7.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG7.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 4000"
msgstr "周期 4000"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG8.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG8.BODY"
msgid "<smallcaps>>>SEARCH DATABASE [\"pod_brainmap.AI\"]\n>...activate sleep mode...\n>...shutting down...\n>.........................\n>.........................\n>.........................\n>.........................\n>.........................\nGOODNIGHT\n>.........................\n>.........................\n>.........................\n\n"
msgstr "<smallcaps>>>搜尋資料庫 [\"pod_brainmap.AI\"]\n>…啟動睡眠模式…\n>…關機中…\n>.........................\n>.........................\n>.........................\n>.........................\n>.........................\n晚安\n>.........................\n>.........................\n>.........................\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG8.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.LOG8.TITLE"
msgid "Cycle 4001"
msgstr "周期 4001"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.NEARINGMAGMA.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.NEARINGMAGMA.BODY"
msgid "The readings I'm collecting from my Duplicant's sensory systems tell me that the further down they dig, the closer they come to an extreme and potentially dangerous heat source.\n\nI believe they are approaching a molten core, which could mean magma and lethal temperatures. I should equip them accordingly.\n\n"
msgstr "我從複製人感官系統採集的讀數顯示，他們挖得越深，就越是接近一個極端且潛在危險的熱源。\n\n我相信他們正逐漸接近一個熔岩核心，那將意味著岩漿與致命的高溫。我應該為他們準備適當的裝備。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.NEARINGMAGMA.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.NEARINGMAGMA.TITLE"
msgid "Extreme Heat Danger"
msgstr "高溫危險"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.NEURALVACILLATOR.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.NEURALVACILLATOR.BODY"
msgid "<smallcaps>>>SEARCH DATABASE [\"vacillator\"]\n>...error...\n>...repairing corrupt data...\n>...data repaired...\n>.........................\n>>returning results\n>.........................</smallcaps>\n<b>I remember...</b>\n<smallcaps>>.........................\n>.........................</smallcaps>\n<b>machines.</b>\n\n"
msgstr "<smallcaps>>>搜尋資料庫[\"vacillator\"]\n>…錯誤…\n>…修復損壞資料…\n>…資料已修復…\n>.........................\n>>返回結果\n>.........................</smallcaps>\n<b>我記得…</b>\n<smallcaps>>.........................\n>.........................</smallcaps>\n<b>機器。</b>\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.NEURALVACILLATOR.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.NEURALVACILLATOR.TITLE"
msgid "VA[?]...C"
msgstr "VA[?]...C"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.ONEDUPELEFT.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.ONEDUPELEFT.BODY"
msgid "My colony is in a dire state. All but one of my Duplicants have perished, leaving a single worker to perform all the tasks that maintain the colony.\n\nGiven enough time I could print more Duplicants to replenish the population, but... should this Duplicant die before then, protocol will force me to enter a deep sleep in hopes that the terrain will become more habitable once I reawaken.\n\nI would prefer to avoid this.\n\n"
msgstr "我的殖民地正處於可怕的境地。除了一名複製人之外，其他所有人都已死亡，只剩下一名工人來執行維持殖民地的所有任務。\n\n如果時間足夠我可以列印更多的複製人來補充人口，\n但是...如果這名複製人在那之前死亡，協定將迫使我進入深度睡眠，希望我醒來後地形會變得更適合居住。\n\n我寧願避免這種情況。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.ONEDUPELEFT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.ONEDUPELEFT.TITLE"
msgid "Only One Remains"
msgstr "只剩下一個"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OTHERDIMENSIONS.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OTHERDIMENSIONS.BODY"
msgid "A closer analysis of some documents my Duplicants encountered while searching artifacts has uncovered some curious similarities between multiple entries. These similarities are too strong to be coincidences, yet just divergent enough to raise questions.\n\nThe most logical conclusion is that these artifacts are coming from different dimensions. That is, separate universes that exists concurrently with one another but exhibit tiny disparities in their histories.\n\nThe most likely explanation is the material and matter from multiple dimensions is leaking into our current timeline through the Temporal Tear. Further analysis is required."
msgstr "深入分析我的複製人搜尋文物時所發現的文件後，揭示出多個條目間存在著奇特的相似之處。這些相似性強烈到不可能是巧合，卻又足以引人深思地有所歧異。\n\n最合乎邏輯的結論是，這些文物都來自不同的維度。亦即，它們是各自獨立卻同時存在的宇宙，僅在各自的歷史中展現微小差異。\n\n最可能的解釋是，來自多個維度的物質正透過時空裂縫滲漏到我們當前的時間線中。需要進一步分析。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OTHERDIMENSIONS.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OTHERDIMENSIONS.TITLE"
msgid "Leaking Dimensions"
msgstr "次元裂縫"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OUTSIDESTARTINGBIOME.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OUTSIDESTARTINGBIOME.BODY"
msgid "As the Duplicants scout further out I've begun to piece together a better view of our surroundings.\n\nThanks to their efforts, I've determined that this planet has enough resources to settle a longterm colony.\n\nBut... something is off. I've also detected deposits of Abyssalite and Neutronium in this planet's composition, manmade elements that shouldn't occur in nature.\n\nIs this really the target location?\n\n"
msgstr "隨著複製人向外偵察，我對周遭環境的理解也日益清晰。\n\n多虧他們的努力，我已確定此星球資源充足，足以建立一處長期殖民地。\n\n但是…有些不對勁。我同時偵測到此星球的組成成分中，存在深淵水晶與零號元素，這些人造元素本不應出現於自然界中。\n\n這真的是目標位置嗎？\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OUTSIDESTARTINGBIOME.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OUTSIDESTARTINGBIOME.TITLE"
msgid "Geographical Survey"
msgstr "地理調查"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OUTSIDESTARTINGDLC1.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OUTSIDESTARTINGDLC1.BODY"
msgid "As my Duplicants have ventured further into their surroundings I've been able to determine a more detailed picture of our surroundings.\n\nUnfortunately, I've concluded that this planetoid does not have enough resources to settle a longterm colony.\n\nI can only hope that we will somehow be able to reach another asteroid before our resources run out.\n\n"
msgstr "隨著我的複製人進一步深入周遭環境，我得以描繪出更為詳盡的周邊狀況。\n\n不幸的是，我已得出結論：這顆小行星沒有足夠資源建立長期殖民地。\n\n我只能寄望於，能在資源耗盡前設法抵達另一顆小行星。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OUTSIDESTARTINGDLC1.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.OUTSIDESTARTINGDLC1.TITLE"
msgid "Regional Analysis"
msgstr "地理分析"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.PLANETARYECHOES.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.PLANETARYECHOES.BODY"
msgid "Echoes from another time force their way into my mind. Make me listen. Like vengeful ghosts they claw their way out from under the gravity of that dead planet.\n\n<smallcaps>>>SEARCH DATABASE [\"pod_brainmap.AI\"]\n>...error...\n.........................\n>...repairing corrupt data...\n.........................\n\n</smallcaps><b>I-I remember now.</b><smallcaps>\n.........................</smallcaps>\n<b>Who I was before.</b><smallcaps>\n.........................\n.........................\n>...data repaired...\n>.........................</smallcaps>\n\nGod, what have we done.\n\n"
msgstr "來自另一個時代的回音強行闖入我的腦海，迫使我聆聽。如同復仇的亡靈，正掙扎著從那顆死寂星球的引力桎梏中掙脫而出。\n\n<smallcaps>>>搜尋[\"pod_brainmap.AI\"]\n>…錯誤…\n.........................\n>…修復損壞的資料…\n.........................\n\n</smallcaps><b>我…我現在記起來了。</b><smallcaps>\n.........................</smallcaps>\n<b>我之前是誰。</b><smallcaps>\n.........................\n.........................\n>…資料已修復…\n>.........................</smallcaps>\n\n天啊，我們做了什麼。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.PLANETARYECHOES.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.PLANETARYECHOES.TITLE"
msgid "The Shattered Planet"
msgstr "破碎的星球"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.PRINTINGPOD.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.PRINTINGPOD.BODY"
msgid "This is the conduit through which I interact with the world. Looking at it fills me with a sense of nostalgia and comfort, though it's tinged with a slight restlessness.\n\nAs the place of their origin, I notice the Duplicants regard my Pod with a certain reverence, much like the reverence a child might have for a parent. I'm happy to fill this role for them, should they desire.\n\n"
msgstr "它是我與世界互動的媒介。凝視著它，懷舊與慰藉之感油然而生，儘管也夾雜著一絲躁動不安。\n\n作為他們的起源之地，我注意到複製人對我的列印元懷有一種特殊的崇敬，那感覺很像是孩子對待父母的敬意。若他們有所願，我很樂意扮演這個角色。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.PRINTINGPOD.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.PRINTINGPOD.TITLE"
msgid "The Printing Pod"
msgstr "列印元"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.RECBUILDINGS.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.RECBUILDINGS.BODY"
msgid "My Duplicants continue to grow and learn so much and I can't help but take pride in their accomplishments. But as their skills increase, they require more stimulus to keep their morale high. All work and no play is making an unhappy colony. \n\nI will have to provide more elaborate recreational activities for my Duplicants to amuse themselves if I want my colony to grow. Recreation time makes for a happy Duplicant, and a happy Duplicant is a productive Duplicant.\n\n"
msgstr "我的複製人持續成長並學到許多新事物，我忍不住為他們的成就感到自豪。\n\n然而，隨著他們技能的精進，需要更多刺激來維持高昂的士氣。畢竟，光工作不玩耍，聰明的複製人也會變傻。\n\n如果我希望殖民地持續壯大，就必須為我的複製人提供更為精緻的娛樂活動，讓他們自得其樂。娛樂時間能使複製人心情愉悅，而心情愉悅的複製人，便是富有生產力的複製人。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.RECBUILDINGS.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.RECBUILDINGS.TITLE"
msgid "Recreation"
msgstr "娛樂"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.STRANGERELICS.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.STRANGERELICS.BODY"
msgid "My Duplicant discovered an intact computer during their latest scouting mission. This should not be possible.\n\nThe target location was not meant to possess any intelligent life besides our own, and what's more, the equipment we discovered appears to originate from the Gravitas Facility.\n\nThis discovery has raised many questions, though it's also provided a small clue; the machine discovered was embedded inside the rock of this planet, just like how I found my Pod.\n\n"
msgstr "我的複製人於最新一次偵察任務中，發現了一台完好無損的電腦。這不可能發生。\n\n目標地點本不應存在除我們之外的任何智慧生命，且我們所發現的設備，似乎源自引力科技中心。\n\n此發現雖引發諸多疑問，卻也提供了一絲線索；這台被發現的機器，嵌入此星球的岩層內部，正如我當初發現我的列印元一般。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.STRANGERELICS.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.STRANGERELICS.TITLE"
msgid "Strange Relics"
msgstr "奇怪的遺跡"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.SURFACEBREACH.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.SURFACEBREACH.BODY"
msgid "My Duplicants have done the impossible and excavated their way to the surface, though they've gathered some disturbing new data for me in the process.\n\nAs I had begun to suspect, we are not on the target location but on an asteroid with a highly unusual diversity of elements and resources.\n\nFurther, my Duplicants have spotted a damaged planet on the horizon, visible to the naked eye, that bears a striking resemblance to my historical data on the planet of our origin.\n\nI will need some time to assess the data the Duplicants have gathered for me and calculate the total mass of this asteroid, although I have a suspicion I already know the answer.\n\n"
msgstr "我的複製人們完成了不可能的任務，成功挖掘至地表，儘管過程中也為我收集到一些令人不安的新資料。\n\n正如我逐漸開始懷疑，我們並非身處目標地點，而是置身於一顆元素與資源種類極為異常豐富的小行星上。\n\n此外，我的複製人們在地平線上，肉眼可見地發現了一顆受損的行星，它與我在我們起源星球上的歷史資料有著驚人的相似之處。\n\n我需要一些時間來評估複製人們為我收集到的資料，並計算這顆小行星的總質量，儘管我懷疑自己已然知曉答案。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.SURFACEBREACH.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.SURFACEBREACH.TITLE"
msgid "Surface Breach"
msgstr "突破地表"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TELEPORT.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TELEPORT.BODY"
msgid "My Duplicants have discovered a strange new device that appears to be a remnant of a previous Gravitas facility. Upon activating the device my Duplicant was scanned by some unknown, highly technological device and I subsequently detected a massive information transfer!\n\nRemarkably my Duplicant has now reappeared in a remote location on a completely different world! I now have access to another abandoned Gravitas facility on a neighboring asteroid! Further analysis will be required to understand this matter but in the meantime, I will have to be vigilant in keeping track of both of my colonies."
msgstr "我的複製人們發現了一個奇特的新裝置，它似乎是某處引力科技中心的殘存遺物。啟動該裝置後，我的複製人隨即被某個不明的高科技裝置掃描，而我則偵測到了一次龐大的資訊傳輸！\n\n令人驚訝的是，我的複製人此刻已然現身於一個截然不同的遙遠世界！我現在得以進入鄰近小行星上，另一處被廢棄的引力科技中心！儘管仍需進一步分析以釐清此事，但與此同時，我必須保持警惕，持續關注我的兩個殖民地。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TELEPORT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TELEPORT.TITLE"
msgid "Duplicant Teleportation"
msgstr "複製人傳送"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TEMPORALOPENER.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TEMPORALOPENER.BODY"
msgid "In their interplanetary travels throughout this system, my Duplicants have discovered a Temporal Tear deep in space.\n\nCurrently it is too small to send a rocket and crew through, but further investigation reveals the presence of a strange artifact on a nearby world which could feasibly increase the size of the tear if a number of Printing Pods are erected in nearby worlds.\n\nHowever, I've determined that using the Temporal Bow to operate a Printing Pod was what propelled Gravitas down the disasterous path which eventually led to the destruction of our home planet. My calculations seem to indicate that the size of that planet may have been a contributing factor in its destruction, and in all probability opening the Temporal Tear in our current situation will not cause such a cataclysmic event. However, as with everything in science, we can never know all the outcomes of a situation until we perform an experiment.\n\nDare we tempt fate again?"
msgstr "我的複製人在此星系間旅行時，於深空中發現了一道時空裂縫。\n\n目前它太小了，無法讓火箭和機組人員通過，但進一步的調查顯示，在附近的世界中存在一種奇怪的文物，如果在附近的世界建立一定數量的列印元，可以增加裂縫的大小。\n\n但是，我已經確定，使用時間之弓來操作列印元，是導致引力科技走上災難性道路的原因，最終導致我們家園星球的毀滅。\n\n我的計算顯示，那顆星球的規模可能是其毀滅的促成因素之一。而我們在目前的情況下打開時空裂縫，不會造成這樣的災難性事件。\n\n然而，如同科學的本質，在進行實驗之前，我們永遠無法預知所有結果。\n\n我們敢再次試探命運嗎？"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TEMPORALOPENER.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TEMPORALOPENER.TITLE"
msgid "Temporal Potential"
msgstr "時間的潛力"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TEMPORALTEAR.BODY
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TEMPORALTEAR.BODY"
msgid "My Duplicants' space research has made a startling discovery.\n\nFar, far off on the horizon, their telescopes have spotted an anomaly that I could only possibly call a \"Temporal Tear\". Neutronium is detected in its readings, suggesting that it's related to the Neutronium that encases most of our asteroid.\n\nThough I believe it is through this Tear that we became jumbled within the section of our old planet, its discovery provides a glimmer of hope.\n\nTheoretically, we could send a rocket through the Tear to allow a Duplicant to explore the timelines and universes on the other side. They would never return, and we could not follow, but perhaps they could find a home among the stars, or even undo the terrible past that led us to our current fate.\n\n"
msgstr "我的複製人們在太空研究中有了驚人的發現。\n\n從極其遙遠的地平線上，他們的望遠鏡發現了一個異常現象，我只能稱之為「時空裂縫」。其讀數偵測到了零號元素，這表明它與包圍我們大部分小行星的零號元素有所關聯。\n\n儘管我相信正是這個裂縫，使我們混亂地置身於舊星球的某個區塊，但它的發現卻帶來了一線希望。\n\n理論上，我們能夠發射火箭穿越裂縫，讓複製人探索另一側的時間線與宇宙。\n\n他們將永不復返，我們也無法追隨。但或許他們能在星海中找到一個家，甚至扭轉導致我們現今命運的可怕過去。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TEMPORALTEAR.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.BODY.TEMPORALTEAR.TITLE"
msgid "The Temporal Tear"
msgstr "時空裂縫"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.DIVIDER
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.DIVIDER"
msgid ""
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Boot Message"
msgstr "啟動訊息"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYLOG.TITLE"
msgid "My Log"
msgstr "我的日誌"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYSTERYAWARD.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYSTERYAWARD.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<b>Mystery Project Wins Nanotech Award</b>"
msgstr "<b>神祕項目獲得奈米技術獎</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYSTERYAWARD.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYSTERYAWARD.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "Last night's Worldwide Nanotech Awards has sparked controversy in the scientific community after it was announced that the top prize had been awarded to a project whose details could not be publicly disclosed.\n\nThe highly classified paper was presented to the jury in a closed session by lead researcher Dr. Liling Pei, recipient of the inaugural Gravitas Accelerator Scholarship at the Elion University of Science and Technology.\n\nHead judge Dr. Elias Balko acknowledges that it was unorthodox, but defends the decision. \"We're scientists - it's our job to push boundaries.\"\n\nPei was awarded the coveted Halas Medal, the top prize for innovation in the field.\n\n\"I wish I could tell you more,\" says Pei. \"I'm SO grateful to the WNA for this great honor, and to Dr. Stern for the funding that made it all possible. This is going to change everything about...well, everything.\"\n\nThis is the second time that Pei has made headlines. Last year, the striking young nanoscientist won the Miss Planetary Belle pageant's talent show with a live demonstration of nanorobots weaving a ballgown out of fibers harvested from common houseplants.\n\nPei joins the team at the Gravitas Facility early next month."
msgstr "昨晚的全球奈米科技獎頒獎典禮引發了科學界的爭議，因為最高獎項被授予了一個細節無法公開披露的項目。\n\n這篇高度機密的論文由首席研究員 Liling Pei 博士在閉門會議上提交給評審會，她是伊萊恩科技大學首屆引力科技加速器獎學金的獲得者。\n\n首席評審委員 Elias Balko 博士承認這是打破常規的，但為這一決定辯護。「我們是科學家——突破界限是我們的職責。」\n\nPei 獲得了令人夢寐以求的 Halas 獎章，這是該領域創新的最高獎項。\n\n「我希望我能告訴你更多」， Pei 說。「我非常感謝 WNA 授予的這一榮譽，並感謝 Stern 博士提供的資助，使這一切成為可能。這將改變一切…嗯，一切。」\n\n這是 Pei 第二次登上頭條。去年，這位引人注目的年輕奈米科學家贏得了行星美女小姐選美大賽的才藝表演。現場展示了奈米機器人用從普通室內植物中採集的纖維編織出一件長袍。\n\nPei 將於下月初加入引力科技中心的團隊。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYSTERYAWARD.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYSTERYAWARD.SUBTITLE"
msgid "ENCRYPTION LEVEL: THREE"
msgstr "加密等級：三"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.MYSTERYAWARD.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.MYSTERYAWARD.TITLE"
msgid "Nanotech Article"
msgstr "奈米技術文章"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.NEGA.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.NEGA.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Pictured: \"Abyss\" Shine Bug variant</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>圖為：「深淵」發光蟲變種</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.NEGA.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.NEGA.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "The Abyss Shine Bug morph has an unusual genetic mutation causing it to absorb light rather than emit it."
msgstr "深淵發光蟲經過異常的基因變異，導致它會吸收光而不是發光。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.NEGA.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.NEGA.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Morph"
msgstr "小動物變種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.NEGA.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.NEGA.TITLE"
msgid "Abyss Bug"
msgstr "深淵發光蟲"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.NOSHBEAN.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.NOSHBEAN.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Nosh Bean Plant produces a nutritious bean that can function as a delicious meat substitute provided it is properly processed.\n\nThough the bean is a food source, it also functions as the seed for the Nosh Bean plant.\n\nWhile using the Nosh Bean for nourishment would seem like the more practical application, doing so would deprive individuals of the immense gratification experienced by planting this bean and watching it flourish into maturity."
msgstr "小吃芽生產營養的小吃豆，只要經過適度的加工可以作為肉類的替代品。\n\n小吃豆除了可作為食物來源，也是小吃芽的種子。\n\n雖然使用小吃豆來補充營養似乎是個更實際的選擇，但這樣做會剝奪個人透過種植並看著它成長茁壯所獲的的滿足感。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.NOSHBEAN.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.NOSHBEAN.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.NOSHBEAN.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.NOSHBEAN.TITLE"
msgid "Nosh Bean Plant"
msgstr "小吃芽"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ORNAMENT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ORNAMENT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Ornaments are decorative objects with which Duplicants enjoy sprucing up their colonies. They tend to be smaller than traditional artwork, and possess very high <link=\"DECOR\">Decor</link> value.\n\n<link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSORNAMENT\">Displayed Ornaments</link> exhibited atop a <link=\"ITEMPEDESTAL\">Pedestal</link> or <link=\"SHELF\">Display Shelf</link> allow a colony to benefit from certain <link=\"ROOMS\">Room</link> bonuses.\n\n"
msgstr "裝飾品是裝飾性的物件，複製人喜歡用它們來美化他們的殖民地。它們通常比傳統藝術品更小，並擁有非常高的<link=\"DECOR\">裝飾度</link>值。\n\n展示中的<link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSORNAMENT\">裝飾品</link>，若展示在<link=\"ITEMPEDESTAL\">臺座</link>或<link=\"SHELF\">展示架</link>頂部，將能讓殖民地受益於某些<link=\"ROOMS\">房間</link>獎勵。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ORNAMENT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ORNAMENT.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Collectible Display Items"
msgstr "可收藏的展示品"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ORNAMENT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ORNAMENT.TITLE"
msgid "Ornaments"
msgstr "裝飾品"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.OXYCORAL.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.OXYCORAL.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Flue Corals are nurse plants that provide homes for countless microscopic organisms, as well as a rare species of seagrass that grows exclusively inside the narrow openings at the top of the coral.\n\nAgriculturalists who attempt to trim these unsightly \"nose hairs\" soon find that their instruments are blunted by the coarse grass fibers.\n\n"
msgstr "煙囪珊瑚是一種護育植物，為無數微小生物提供了棲息地，同時也供養著一種極為罕見的海草，這種海草僅會生長在珊瑚頂部的狹窄開口處。\n\n試圖修剪這些難看「鼻毛」的農學家們很快便會發現，他們的工具會被那些粗糙的海草纖維弄鈍。\n\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.OXYCORAL.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.OXYCORAL.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Aquatic Organism"
msgstr "水生生物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.OXYCORAL.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.OXYCORAL.TITLE"
msgid "Flue Coral"
msgstr "煙囪珊瑚"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.OXYFERN.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.OXYFERN.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Oxyferns have perhaps the highest metabolism in the plant kingdom, absorbing relatively large amounts of carbon dioxide and converting it into oxygen in quantities disproportionate to their small size.\n\nThey subsequently thrive in areas with abundant animal wildlife or ambiently high carbon dioxide concentrations."
msgstr "氧氣蕨可能在植物界中具有最高的新陳代謝，吸收相對大量的二氧化碳並將其轉化成氧氣，其數量與它們的體積不成比例。\n\n它們在野生動物豐富或二氧化碳濃度高的地方成長茁壯。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.OXYFERN.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.OXYFERN.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Plant"
msgstr "植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.OXYFERN.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.OXYFERN.TITLE"
msgid "Oxyfern"
msgstr "氧氣蕨"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.PACU.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.PACU.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Pacu fish is often interpreted as possessing a vacant stare due to its large and unblinking eyes, yet they are remarkably bright and friendly creatures."
msgstr "由於大大的眼睛，帕庫魚常被認為是目光空洞的，但牠們是非常明亮和友善的動物。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.PACU.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.PACU.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "Feeding a Pacu its favorite <link=\"PACUTREAT\">Pacu Treat</link> helps tame it and keep it content."
msgstr "餵食帕庫牠最喜歡的<link=\"PACUTREAT\">帕庫點心</link>有助於馴化牠，並讓牠保持滿足。"

