#. STRINGS.CODEX.ROVER.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ROVER.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Rover is a planetary scout robot programmed to land on and mine Planetoids where sending a Duplicant would put them unneccessarily in danger.\n\nRovers are programmed to be very pleasant and social when interacting with other beings. However, an unintended consequence of this programming is that the socialized robots tended to experience the same work slow-downs due to loneliness and low morale.\n\nTo compensate for this, the Rover was programmed to have two distinct personalities it can switch between to have pleasant in-depth conversations with itself during long stints alone."
msgstr "漫遊者是一種星球探測機器人，被設計用來登陸並開採小行星。將複製人送到這些地方，會使他們陷入不必要的危險中。\n\n漫遊者被設計為與其它生物互動社交會很愉快。然而，這種設計的結果是，社交化機器人往往會因為孤獨與低士氣，而經歷相同的工作倦怠。\n\n為了彌補這一點，漫遊者被程式設定為具有兩種不同的性格，它可以在兩種不同的性格之間切換，以便在長時間獨處時與自己進行愉快的深入對話。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ROVER.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ROVER.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Scouting Robot"
msgstr "探測機器人"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ROVER.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ROVER.TITLE"
msgid "Rover"
msgstr "漫遊者"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ROYAL.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ROYAL.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Pictured: \"Royal\" Shine Bug variant</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>圖為：「王室」發光蟲變種</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ROYAL.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ROYAL.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "The Shine Bug can be pet anywhere else along its body, although it is advised that care still be taken due to the generally delicate nature of its exoskeleton."
msgstr "發光蟲可以飼養在除了自己身體以外的任何地方，雖然只是建議但仍然需要小心照顧，因為它的外骨骼通常很脆弱。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ROYAL.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ROYAL.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Morph"
msgstr "小動物變種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.ROYAL.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.ROYAL.TITLE"
msgid "Royal Bug"
msgstr "王室發光蟲"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SAGE.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SAGE.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Pictured: \"Sage\" Hatch variant</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>圖為：「草食」哈奇變種</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SAGE.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SAGE.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "It is difficult to classify the Hatch's diet as the term \"omnivore\" does not extend to the non-organic materials it is capable of ingesting.\n\nA more appropriate term is \"totumvore\", given that it can consume and find nutritional value in nearly every known substance."
msgstr "難以替哈奇的飲食進行分類，因為專業術語上所謂的「雜食動物」未包含非有機材料。\n\n更合適的術語是「全食性動物」，因為牠可以食用並找到所有已知物質的營養價值。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SAGE.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SAGE.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Morph"
msgstr "小動物變種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SAGE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SAGE.TITLE"
msgid "Sage Hatch"
msgstr "草食哈奇"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SALTYSTICKSPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SALTYSTICKSPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Sodicane plant is a hardy member of the Poaceae family of grasses, well-suited to amateur farmers in warm climates.\n\nWhile the crystallized mineral deposits on its stalks are quite palatable, they can only be eaten by gnawing on the unfortunately fibrous stalk."
msgstr "鹹蔗是一種頑強的禾本科植物，非常適合溫暖氣候下的業餘農民種植。\n\n雖然植株莖上附著的結晶礦物相當可口，但必須透過啃咬那不幸且充滿纖維的莖部才能食用。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SALTYSTICKSPLANT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SALTYSTICKSPLANT.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SALTYSTICKSPLANT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SALTYSTICKSPLANT.TITLE"
msgid "Sodicane"
msgstr "鹹蔗"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SATURNCRITTERTRAP.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SATURNCRITTERTRAP.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Saturn Critter Trap plant is a carnivorous plant that lays in wait for unsuspecting critters to happen by, then traps them in its mouth for consumption.\n\nThe Saturn Trap Plant's predatory mechanism is reflective of the harsh radioactive habitat it resides in.\n\nOnce trapped in the deadly maw of the plant, creatures are gently asphyxiated then digested through powerful acidic enzymes which coat the inner sides of the Saturn Trap Plant's leaves."
msgstr "捕獸草是一種食肉植物，它們會等待毫無防備的小動物經過，然後將它們困在嘴裡吃掉。\n\n捕獸草的捕食機制反映出了它所處的輻射棲息地。\n\n一旦被困在植物致命的喉嚨裡、小動物會慢慢窒息然後被捕獸草葉子內側的強酸所消化。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SATURNCRITTERTRAP.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SATURNCRITTERTRAP.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Carnivorous Plant"
msgstr "食肉植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SATURNCRITTERTRAP.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SATURNCRITTERTRAP.TITLE"
msgid "Saturn Critter Trap"
msgstr "捕獸草"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SCHOOLNEWSPAPER.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SCHOOLNEWSPAPER.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<b>Party Time for Local Students</b>"
msgstr "<b>本地學生的派對時間</b>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SCHOOLNEWSPAPER.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SCHOOLNEWSPAPER.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "Students at the Elion University of Science and Technology have held an unconventional party this weekend.\n\nWhile their peers may have been out until the wee hours wearing lampshades on their heads and drawing eyebrows on sleeping colleagues, students Jackie Stern and Olivia Broussard spent the weekend in their dorm, refreshments and decorations ready, waiting for the arrival of the guests of honor: themselves.\n\nThe two prospective STEM students, who study theoretical physics with a focus on the workings of space time, conducted the experiment under the assumption that, were their theories about the malleability of space time to ever come to fruition, their future selves could travel back in time to greet them at the party, proving the existence of time travel.\n\nThey weren't inconsiderate of their future selves' busy schedules though; should the guests of honor be unable to attend, they were encouraged to send back a message using the codeword \"Hourglass\" to communicate that, while they certainly wanted to come, they were simply unable.\n\nSadly no one RSVP'd or arrived to the party, but that did not dishearten Olivia or Jackie.\n\nAs Olivia put it, \"It just meant more snacks for us!\""
msgstr "在伊萊恩科技大學的學生們在本周末舉行了一場非傳統的舞會。\n\n雖然她們的同齡人可能一直玩到凌晨，頭上戴著燈罩，在睡著的同事身上畫眉毛。學生 Jackie Stern 和 Olivia Broussard 卻在她們的宿舍裡度過了週末，準備好了茶點和裝飾，等待著貴賓的到來：她們自己。\n\n這兩名潛心研究時間和空間運作的理論物理學的準 STEM 學生，在一個假設下進行了這個實驗：如果她們關於時空可變性的理論有一天實現了，那麼她們未來的自我可以穿越時空回到過去來參加派對，證明時間旅行的存在。\n\n她們並沒有考慮到她們未來自我繁忙的排程安排；如果貴賓無法出席，她們被鼓勵使用暗號「沙漏」發送回信息，以表明她們確實想來，但她們只是單純地做不到。\n\n遺憾的是沒有人回覆或出席這個派對，但這並沒使 Olivia 或 Jackie 感到沮喪。\n\n正如 Olivia 所說，「這對我們來說意味著有更多的小吃可以吃了！」"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SCHOOLNEWSPAPER.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SCHOOLNEWSPAPER.SUBTITLE"
msgid "ENCRYPTION LEVEL: THREE"
msgstr "加密等級：三"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SCHOOLNEWSPAPER.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SCHOOLNEWSPAPER.TITLE"
msgid "Campus Newspaper Article"
msgstr "校園報紙文章"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "\"Kelpole\" is the colloquial name given to <i>Osculateus venerandum</i>, a small free-moving organism spawned from microscopic eggs that attach themselves to <link=\"SEATREE\">Tower Kelp</link>.\n\nThese unusual critters possess only a few hundred neurons and rely primarily on leaf mimicry to camouflage them from predators during their brief lives.\n\nFormerly considered flora, Kelpoles were eventually reclassified as fauna due to their frequent inclusion on marine biologists' lists of top ten most adorable creatures. The term \"flona\" was rejected out of hand."
msgstr "「藻蝌蚪」是<i>維內蘭杜姆吻蟲 (Osculateus venerandum)</i> 的俗稱，這是一種自由活動的小型生物，由附著在<link=\"SEATREE\">塔藻</link>上的微小卵孵化而來。\n\n這些奇特的小動物僅擁有數百個神經元，在其短暫的一生中，主要依賴模仿葉片進行偽裝，以躲避捕食者。\n\n藻蝌蚪曾被視為植物，但因其屢次登上海洋生物學家的「十大最可愛生物」榜單，最終被重新歸類為動物。「植動體 (flona)」一詞在提出後便遭直接駁回。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Aquatic Organism"
msgstr "水生生物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Kelpole"
msgstr "藻蝌蚪類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Aquatic Critter"
msgstr "水生小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAFAIRY.TITLE"
msgid "Kelpole"
msgstr "藻蝌蚪"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAHORSE.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAHORSE.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Adult Seaquines flood their brood pouches with <link=\"FISHMILK\">Ovolene</link> to nourish their eggs and support osmoregulation.\n\nAs this is an energy-intensive process, it is abandoned in later life stages so that geriatric Seaquine can focus their efforts on laying one final egg before they perish."
msgstr "成年海馬會向育兒囊中注入<link=\"FISHMILK\">卵漿</link>，以滋養受精卵並輔助滲透壓調節。\n\n由於此過程極耗能量，海馬在生命晚期會停止分泌，以便將剩餘精力集中於產下臨終前的最後一枚卵。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAHORSE.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAHORSE.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Species"
msgstr "小動物物種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAHORSE.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAHORSE.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Seaquine"
msgstr "海馬類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAHORSE.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAHORSE.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Aquatic Critter"
msgstr "水生小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAHORSE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAHORSE.TITLE"
msgid "Seaquine"
msgstr "海馬"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAL.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAL.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Spigot Seals are named for the hollow, cone-shaped glabellar protrusion that allows them to siphon nourishment directly from plants into the digestive sac located at the cone's base.\n\nIn order to draw nutritious fluids through this \"straw,\" the Spigot Seal compresses its nasal cavity and pumps its tongue up into its soft palate repeatedly, creating a vacuum.\n\nMealtimes are concluded by lapping at the air to reopen the airways and prevent accidental asphyxiation.\n\nMany handlers enjoy teaching this critter to clap its flippers, only to discover that there is no reliable method of limiting how often or how loudly the behavior is repeated."
msgstr "栓角海豹因其中空的錐形眉間突起物而得名，這種結構能讓牠們直接從植物中吸取營養，流入位於錐形底部的消化囊中。\n\n為了透過這根「吸管」吸取營養液，栓角海豹會壓緊鼻腔，並將舌頭反覆抽入其軟顎，形成真空。\n\n進食結束時，透過快速舔食空氣重新開啟氣道，從而防止發生意外窒息。\n\n許多飼養員喜歡教這種小動物拍打腳蹼，卻發現沒有可靠辦法限制這種行為的重複頻率和聲音大小。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAL.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAL.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Domesticable Species"
msgstr "可馴化的物種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAL.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAL.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Spigot Seals"
msgstr "角海豹類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAL.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAL.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Domesticable Critter"
msgstr "可馴養的小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAL.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAL.TITLE"
msgid "Spigot Seal"
msgstr "栓角海豹"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEATREE.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEATREE.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "This species of the Laminariales order is composed of vertical stems supported by structural vines. What appear to be leaves are actually <link=\"SEAFAIRYSPECIES\">Kelpoles</link>, aquatic critters that consume aeronutrients present in the Tower Kelp's hollow stalk.\n\nTower Kelp stalks that fail to attract these natural pressure regulators will collapse before reaching maturation."
msgstr "此種海帶目物種，由豎直的主莖與起支撐作用的構造藤蔓所組成。那些看似葉片的部位，實際上是<link=\"SEAFAIRYSPECIES\">藻蝌蚪</link>——一種以塔藻中空莖稈內的氣態養分為食的水生生物。\n\n若塔藻的莖稈未能吸引這些天然的壓力調節者，便會在成熟前坍塌。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEATREE.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEATREE.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Cultivable Plant"
msgstr "可耕種植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEATREE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEATREE.TITLE"
msgid "Tower Kelp"
msgstr "塔藻"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEATURTLE.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEATURTLE.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Orehulls are oversized anamniotes prized for the iron ore deposits that adorn their carapace.\n\nSpecialized glands between the carapace scutes continuously release microscopic amounts of the heavy metals present in the critter's environment, an immune system reaction that causes no discomfort to the Orehull.\n\n"
msgstr "礦甲龜是一種體型巨大的無羊膜動物，因其甲殼上附著的鐵礦沉積物而備受珍視。\n\n位於甲殼鱗片之間的特化腺體，會持續釋放環境中殘留的微量重金屬；這是一種免疫系統反應，對礦甲龜本身並不會造成任何不適。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEATURTLE.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEATURTLE.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Species"
msgstr "小動物物種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEATURTLE.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEATURTLE.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Orehull"
msgstr "礦甲龜類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEATURTLE.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEATURTLE.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Aquatic Critter"
msgstr "水生小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEATURTLE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEATURTLE.TITLE"
msgid "Orehull"
msgstr "礦甲龜"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAURCHIN.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAURCHIN.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Pinpoki are prized by marine cuisine gourmands for their delicate buttery flesh, with an aftertaste that some describe as \"transcendant.\"\n\nThe flavor is so legendary that even just gazing upon a displayed Pinpoki is enough to inspire a high level of emotional satisfaction."
msgstr "針膽因其細緻如奶油般的肉質，以及被部分食客形容為「超越凡俗」的餘韻，而備受海洋美食家們的推崇。\n\n其風味堪稱傳奇，甚至僅僅是凝視著一顆展示中的針膽，便足以為人帶來高度的情緒滿足感。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAURCHIN.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAURCHIN.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Aquatic Organism"
msgstr "水生生物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SEAURCHIN.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEAURCHIN.TITLE"
msgid "Pinpoki"
msgstr "針膽"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SHERBERRY.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SHERBERRY.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The semi-parasitic Sherberry plant leeches moisture and trace minerals from the primordial ice formations in which it grows.\n\nThe fruit of this varietal contains low levels of stomach-upsetting phoratoxins which, while not fatal, do serve as strong motivation for foragers to seek out additional sources of nutrition."
msgstr "半寄生雪莓植物從其生長的原始冰層中吸取水分和微量礦物質。具有強大的動力尋找額外的營養來源。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SHERBERRY.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SHERBERRY.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SHERBERRY.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SHERBERRY.TITLE"
msgid "Sherberry Plant"
msgstr "雪漿果藤"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SHINEBUG.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SHINEBUG.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The bioluminescence of the Shine Bug's body serves the social purpose of finding and communicating with others of its kind."
msgstr "發光蟲生物冷光的身體，是用來尋找同伴並進行溝通的。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SHINEBUG.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SHINEBUG.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Species"
msgstr "動物類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SHINEBUG.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SHINEBUG.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Shine Bugs"
msgstr "發光蟲類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SHINEBUG.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SHINEBUG.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Domesticable Critter"
msgstr "可馴養的小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SHINEBUG.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SHINEBUG.TITLE"
msgid "Shine Bug"
msgstr "發光蟲"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SLEETWHEAT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SLEETWHEAT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Sleet Wheat plant has become so well-adapted to cold environments, it is no longer able to survive at room temperatures."
msgstr "雪地小麥適應在寒冷的環境下生長，它不能在室溫下存活。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SLEETWHEAT.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SLEETWHEAT.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "The grain of the Sleet Wheat can be ground down into high quality foodstuffs, or planted to cultivate further Sleet Wheat plants."
msgstr "雪地小麥的穀粒磨碎後可製成高品質的食物，或栽種後會成長為雪地小麥。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SLEETWHEAT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SLEETWHEAT.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SLEETWHEAT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SLEETWHEAT.TITLE"
msgid "Sleet Wheat"
msgstr "雪地小麥"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SLICKSTER.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SLICKSTER.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Slicksters are a unique creature most renowned for their ability to exude hydrocarbon waste that is nearly identical in makeup to crude oil.\n\nThe two tufts atop a Slickster's head are called rhinophores, and help guide the Slickster toward breathable carbon dioxide."
msgstr "小油怪是一種獨特的動物，以排放與石油幾乎相同的廢棄物而聞名。\n\n小油怪頭部突出的兩個觸角是化學接收器，幫助找到可呼吸的二氧化碳。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SLICKSTER.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SLICKSTER.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Species"
msgstr "動物類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SLICKSTER.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SLICKSTER.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Slicksters"
msgstr "小滑頭類"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SLICKSTER.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SLICKSTER.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Domesticable Critter"
msgstr "可馴養的小動物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SLICKSTER.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SLICKSTER.TITLE"
msgid "Slickster"
msgstr "小油怪"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SMOOTH.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SMOOTH.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Pictured: \"Smooth\" Hatch variant</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>圖為：「金屬」哈奇變種</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SMOOTH.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SMOOTH.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "The proper way to pet a Hatch is to touch any of its four feet to first make it aware of your presence, then either scratch the soft segmented underbelly or firmly pat the creature's thick chitinous back."
msgstr "飼養哈奇寵物的正確方式是，先觸碰牠們四隻腳的任一隻讓牠知道你的存在，然後撫摸柔軟的腹部或是拍打有著堅硬角質層的後背。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SMOOTH.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SMOOTH.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Morph"
msgstr "小動物變種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SMOOTH.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SMOOTH.TITLE"
msgid "Smooth Hatch"
msgstr "金屬哈奇"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SNAIL.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SNAIL.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Slogos' unusually thick skin prevents them from succumbing to the fatal osmosis that other members of the Gastropoda class experience after exposure to <link=\"SALT\">Salt</link>.\n\n"
msgstr "緩螺異常厚實的皮膚，使其免於遭受致命的滲透壓作用，而這通常是其他腹足綱生物在接觸<link=\"SALT\">鹽</link>後會面臨的命運。\n"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SNAIL.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SNAIL.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "This enables them to safely enjoy the fluid retention properties of their preferred food."
msgstr "正因如此，它們得以安全享受其喜愛食物所具有的水分滯留特性。"

