#. STRINGS.CODEX.SPACEARTIFACT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SPACEARTIFACT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "While out harvesting resources from space POIs, miners may discover rare artifacts that pique their interest.\n\nThese can be gathered and transported back to the colony using a rocket equipped with an <link=\"ARTIFACTCARGOBAY\">Artifact Transport Module</link>."
msgstr "在從太空興趣點收穫資源的過程中，採礦者可能會發現引起他們興趣的稀有文物。\n\n這些文物可以使用配備了<link=\"ARTIFACTCARGOBAY\">文物運輸模組</link>的火箭，收集並運回殖民地。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SPACEARTIFACT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SPACEARTIFACT.TITLE"
msgid "Space Artifacts"
msgstr "太空文物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SPACETREE.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SPACETREE.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "The Bonbon Tree is a towering plant developed to thrive in below-freezing temperatures. It features multiple independently functioning branches that synthesize bright light to funnel nutrients into a hollow central core.\n\nOnce the tree is fully grown, the core secretes digestive enzymes that break down surplus nutrients and store them as thick, sweet fluid. This can be refined into <link=\"SUCROSE\">Sucrose</link> for the production of higher-tier foods, or used as-is to sustain Spigot Seal ranches.\n\nBonbon Trees are generally considered an eyesore, and would likely be eradicated if not for their delicious output."
msgstr "糖心樹是一種高聳的植物，可以在零下溫度中茁壯成長。它具有多個獨立運作的分枝，透過合成光線將營養物質彙集到中空的中心核中。\n\n這種植物完全成熟後，核心部位就會分泌消化酵素，能將多餘的營養物質分解並以黏稠、甜蜜的液體形態儲存。這種液體可以提煉成<link=\"SUCROSE\">蔗糖</link>，用於生產更高階的食物，或直接用於維持栓角海豹養殖。\n\n糖心樹通常被認為是有礙觀瞻，如果沒有美味的產出物，很有可能會被根除。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SPACETREE.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SPACETREE.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SPACETREE.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SPACETREE.TITLE"
msgid "Bonbon Tree"
msgstr "糖心樹"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SPINDLYGRUBFRUITPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SPINDLYGRUBFRUITPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Spindly Grubfruit Plants have leggy stems that limit the distribution of nutrients and enzymes to the fruit-bearing branch. This results in a reliable but relatively tasteless harvest.\n\nIntroducing the <link=\"DIVERGENTSPECIES\">Divergent</link> critter species to these plants enable them to develop into <link=\"SUPERWORMPLANT\">Grubfruit Plants</link> with stronger vascular systems and improved fruit."
msgstr "蕪弱蟲蜜草細長的莖限制了營養物質和酶向結果枝條的分佈。這導致了可靠但相對無味的果實。\n\n將<link=\"DIVERGENTSPECIES\">變異蟲</link>引入這些植物附近，可以使其發育成<link=\"SUPERWORMPLANT\">蟲蜜草</link>，具有更強的維管系統與更高品質的果實。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SPINDLYGRUBFRUITPLANT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SPINDLYGRUBFRUITPLANT.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr "可食用植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SPINDLYGRUBFRUITPLANT.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SPINDLYGRUBFRUITPLANT.TITLE"
msgid "Spindly Grubfruit Plant"
msgstr "蕪弱蟲蜜草"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SPORECHID.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SPORECHID.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Sporechids take advantage of their flower's attractiveness to lure unsuspecting victims into clouds of parasitic Zombie Spores.\n\nThey are a rare form of holoparasitic plant which finds mammalian hosts to infect rather than the usual plant species.\n\nThe Zombie Spore was originally designed for medicinal purposes but its sedative properties were never refined to the point of usefulness."
msgstr "惡魔花利用它們的花朵引誘沒有戒心的受害者到殭屍孢子雲中。\n\n它們是一種罕見的全寄生植物，它找到哺乳動物宿主感染而不是普通的植物物種。\n\n殭屍孢子最初設計用於藥用目的，但其鎮靜特性從未被提煉到有用的程度。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SPORECHID.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SPORECHID.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Poisonous Plant"
msgstr "有毒植物"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SPORECHID.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SPORECHID.TITLE"
msgid "Sporechid"
msgstr "惡魔花"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SQUEAKY.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SQUEAKY.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "<smallcaps>Pictured: \"Squeaky\" Puft variant</smallcaps>"
msgstr "<smallcaps>圖為：「氯氣」帕夫變種</smallcaps>"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SQUEAKY.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SQUEAKY.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid "Pufts often have a collection of asymmetric teeth lining the ridge of their mouths, although this feature is entirely vestigial as Pufts do not consume solid food.\n\nInstead, a baleen-like mesh of keratin at the back of the Puft's throat works to filter out tiny organisms and food particles from the air.\n\nUnusable air is expelled back out the Puft's posterior trunk, along with waste material and any indigestible particles or pathogens which it then evacuates as solid biomass."
msgstr "帕夫的嘴裡通常有整排不對稱的牙齒，雖然這是個退化的特徵，但牠們也不吃固體食物。\n\n取而代之的是，帕夫嘴巴內有著角蛋白形成的網狀物可以過濾微生物與食物粒子。\n\n不可用的空氣從帕夫的身體後面排出，難以消化並含有病菌的固體排泄物也會一併排出。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SQUEAKY.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SQUEAKY.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Morph"
msgstr "小動物變種"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SQUEAKY.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SQUEAKY.TITLE"
msgid "Squeaky Puft"
msgstr "氯氣帕夫"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SQUID.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SQUID.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid "Glo Squids are immediately recognizable by the bioluminescent photophores that strobe vertically along their soft bodies.\n\nThese tropical critters are distant relatives of the <i>Euprymna scolopes</i>, though rather than navigating via jet propulsion, Glo Squids have evolved a pair of elongated tentacles that enable them to swim upright.\n\n"
msgstr "彩斑魷柔軟的軀體上，垂直分佈著閃爍的生物發光器，因此極易辨識。\n\n這些熱帶小動物是<i>夏威夷短尾魷魚 (Euprymna scolopes)</i> 的遠親，不過與後者不同，牠們並非依靠噴射推進，而是演化出了一對細長的觸手，使其能夠直立游動。"

#. STRINGS.CODEX.SQUID.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SQUID.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter Species"
msgstr "小動物物種"

